\par\par \b \uc2 Crypto Price Analysis 1-14 BITCOIN: BTC, ETHEREUM: ETH, SOLANA: SOL, RIPPLE: XRP, ARBITRUM: ARB, FILECOIN: FIL, INJECTIVE: INJ\b0\par\par\uc2 Amara Khatri \par \uc2 2,597 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 January 2025\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2025, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Drop Sparks Market Crash Fears}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Litecoin (LTC) Plunges After X Account Hack}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Institutional Crypto OTC Volumes Doubled in 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MicroStrategy Purchases Additional Bitcoin}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ripple (XRP) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arbitrum (ARB) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Filecoin (FIL) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Injective (INJ) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) briefly plummeted below $90,000 on Monday, ringing alarm bells among investors as markets panicked. However, it quickly rebounded from this level to reach $92,500 and then climbed to its current level of $95,400. Despite the drop, BTC is up just over 1% in the past 24 hours.\par \par \uc2 Price action was mixed for other cryptocurrencies, with some registering notable increases while others dropped considerably. Ethereum (ETH) is down almost 2% in the past 24 hours and has declined nearly 14% over the past week. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/TRX-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tron (TRX)}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/XLM-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stellar (XLM)}}}\uc2 , Uniswap (UNI), and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/LTC-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Litecoin (LTC)}}}\uc2  have also registered notable drops. Meanwhile, \uc2 Solana\uc2  (SOL), Ripple (XRP), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/DOGE-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE)}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/ADA-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano (\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 )}}}\uc2 , Sui, and Toncoin (TON) have reported a jump in prices. The crypto market cap is marginally down and currently sits at $3.28 trillion.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Drop Sparks Market Crash Fears\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2025/01/crypto-price-analysis-1-13-bitcoin-btc-ethereum-eth-solana-sol-dogecoin-doge-dogwifhatwif-algorand-algo-celestia-tia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  brief plunge below $91,000 sparked significant panic in the market about an impending price crash. BTC has been in the doldrums since its post-election peak. The drop came despite Trump promising a crypto-friendly administration and making Bitcoin a central theme of his policy. Despite the promises and initial optimism, analysts are still worried about a price crash. Alex Kuptsikevich, FxPro Chief Market Analyst, stated,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe start of the new year has not been easy for the crypto market. The next target for the bears looks to be the $88,000 area. And in a negative scenario, bitcoin will face a quick pullback to $74,000.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 BTC and the crypto market have struggled to build momentum after December\u8217\'20\'19s highs thanks to a string of positive economic indicators and updates, indicating the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will be less likely to reduce interest rates this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLosing over 2% in 24 hours to $3.22 trillion, the market was back at the bottom of the consolidation range since the end of November. The promising start to the year failed to materialize. It is with some trepidation that we now watch the eighth or so attempt to break below $3.20 trillion. Adding to the unease is the fact that last week's upside momentum failed to develop, only attracting sellers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  (LTC) Plunges After X Account Hack\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  (LTC) dropped 4% as it struggled to recover from a recent hack that eroded confidence in the asset. The breach occurred when hackers compromised \uc2 Litecoin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s official X account and gained access to promote a fraudulent LTC token. The hackers falsely claimed the token was a Solana-hosted initiative. While the hack did not compromise the \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  network, the incident has significantly amplified the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment across LTC spot markets.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) and SUI have also reported double-digit losses as traders take profits after last week\u8217\'20\'19s rally. The drop indicates caution among traders as the market faces broader \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment as the release of the US CPI data looms.\par \par \uc2 Institutional Crypto OTC Volumes Doubled in 2024\par \par \uc2 Institutional Over-The-Counter (OTC) trading volumes registered a jump of 106% in 2024, driven by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s US election victory and growing demand for spot crypto ETFs. The fourth quarter saw the largest jump, with Bitcoin (BTC), Ethereum (ETH), and stablecoin trading volumes rising 80%, 187%, and 191% year-on-year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough comprehensive regulatory clarity is still pending, the pro-crypto stance of the Trump administration significantly fueled Q4 crypto spot trading to 2024 highs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The second quarter registered a 110% year-on-year increase, which Finery Markets attributed to the launch of spot Bitcoin ETFs. The growth in institutional crypto OTC volumes is due to TradFi financial leaders shifting their stance from skepticism to neutrality.\par \par \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2  Purchases Additional Bitcoin\par \par \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2  has added another 2,530 BTC to its reserves, according to an 8-K filing with the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC). The company acquired its latest tranche of the asset for $243 million, putting the average price of each BTC around $95,972. The latest acquisition marks the tenth consecutive week the company has acquired BTC. \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2  intends to raise $42 billion by 2027 through convertible debt offerings and at-the-market stock sales to fund further BTC purchases.\par \par \uc2 However, analysts are divided about \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s BTC acquisition strategy. Some have raised concerns about the long-term sustainability of its debt and equity-fueled purchases. Financial analyst Jacob King warned of the risks, stating,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s business model is a giant scam and relies on a reflexive loop: it issues debt or equity to buy BTC, which drives BTC\u8217\'20\'19s price higher. This increases MSTR\u8217\'20\'19s market cap, boosts its index weight, and attracts more sheep investors. With a higher valuation, it issues more equity to buy even more BTC. The cycle only works if BTC keeps rising. If BTC stalls or crashes (which it will), the loop collapses. This is unsustainable and is a giant Ponzi..\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/BTC-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  outlook remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite briefly dipping below $90,000 on Monday. Analysts explained that BTC\u8217\'20\'19s recent price action is driven by the strengthening dollar, supported by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hawkish stance and concerns about Tariffs. However, despite macroeconomic challenges, the outlook for the flagship currency remains structurally \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to Grayscale\u8217\'20\'19s research director, Zach Pandl. Pandl believes recent price action could temporarily halt BTC. However, the upcoming presidential inauguration could create positive momentum in the market.\par \par \uc2 Analysts are relatively optimistic about BTC in 2025. Steno Research predicts it will reach new all-time highs thanks to a favorable regulatory environment, leading to more institutional adoption. BTC faced significant selling pressure on Monday, as seen in the price chart, with the asset struggling to build momentum after dropping below the 20 and 50-day SMAs. BTC was \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the first week of the new year, going above the 20 and 50-day SMAs on Friday (January 3). The price registered marginal increases on Saturday and Sunday, settling at $98,309. BTC started the previous week on a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  note, rising almost 4% to go above $100,000 and settling at $102,228.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/3fiMZRUr/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, market sentiment changed on Tuesday as BTC fell below the 50-day SMA after a drop of over 5% and settled at $97,019. The price fell below the 20-day SMA on Wednesday, dropping to an intraday low of $92,546 before recovering to settle at $95,121, dropping almost 2%. Sellers retained control on Thursday as the price fell 2.53% to $92,710. Buyers returned to the market on Friday as BTC registered an increase of over 2%. However, it could not move beyond the 20-day SMA and ultimately settled at $94,818. The weekend saw BTC register a marginal decline on Saturday and a marginal increase on Sunday to settle at $94,585. BTC crashed on Monday, dipping below $90,000 as it fell to an intraday low of $89,397.\par \par \uc2 However, it recovered from this level to reclaim $90,000 and move to $94,492. The current session sees BTC marginally up as buyers look to reclaim $95,000 and move towards $100,000.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/ETH-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH)}}}\uc2  briefly slipped below $3,000 on Monday as markets plummeted following fears of a price collapse. ETH had begun a recovery during the first week of the new year, as its momentum carried it beyond the 20 and 50-day SMAs. As a result, the price crossed the crucial $3,500 level on Friday and rose to $3,657 on Saturday. However, it registered a marginal decline on Sunday to end the weekend at $3,634. ETH picked up on Monday, rising 1.46% to $3,687. Despite a positive start to the week, ETH plummeted on Tuesday, dropping over 8% to go below the 20 and 50-day SMAs and settled at $3,381. The price dropped to an intraday low of $3,217 on Wednesday but recovered to settle at $3,327.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/r8Xev5uO/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Sellers retained control on Thursday as ETH dropped just over 3% to $3,220. Buyers returned to the market on Friday as ETH registered an increase of 1.45% and moved to $3,267. The weekend began with ETH experiencing \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Saturday as buyers and sellers struggled to establish control. Buyers ultimately gained the upper hand as ETH registered a marginal increase and moved to $3,283. However, it dropped on Sunday to end the weekend at $3,266. The ETH price collapsed on Monday as it plummeted to an intraday low of $2,930, slipping below the 200-day SMA. It recovered from this level to reclaim $3,000 and settle at $3,137, ultimately registering a drop of almost 4%. The current session sees ETH up 1.34% and trading around $3,179 as buyers attempt to reclaim lost ground and push the price towards $3,500.\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  (SOL) reached an intraday high of $223 last Monday as it attempted to move past the 50-day SMA. However, with sellers active at this level, it lost momentum, dropping over 7% to $202 on Tuesday. The price continued to fall on Wednesday, slipping below the 20-day SMA to an intraday low of $188 before recovering and settling at $197, above the 20-day SMA. Selling pressure intensified on Thursday as SOL slipped below the 20-day SMA after a drop of over 6% and settled at $185. Buyers returned to the market on Friday, pushing SOL to an intraday high of $193 before settling at $187.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/REK4dtrf/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL experienced considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the weekend as buyers and sellers struggled to establish control. Buyers ultimately gained the upper hand as SOL registered marginal increases on Saturday and Sunday to end the weekend at $188. Markets turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday as SOL dropped to an intraday low of $169, briefly going below key support levels and the 200-day SMA. However, it recovered from this level to reclaim $180 and settle at $182, ultimately registering a drop of almost 3%. The current session sees SOL up 2.33% as buyers look to push it above the 20-day SMA and $200. SOL must first cross the resistance at $190 for this to happen.\par \par \uc2 Ripple (XRP) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/XRP-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ripple (XRP)}}}\uc2  is defying market trends as it looks to push toward $3 after finding support at the 20-day SMA. XRP had moved past the 20-day SMA on January 1 and reached an intraday high of $2.47 by Friday (December 3). However, it lost momentum over the weekend, dropping 1.35% on Saturday and 0.90% on Sunday to settle at $2.39. XRP could only register an increase of 0.92% on Monday before dropping over 6% on Tuesday and settling at $2.27. XRP recovered on Wednesday, thanks to the 20-day SMA acting as a dynamic support level, rising 4.48% to $2.37. The price fell back on Thursday, dropping just over 4% to $2.27.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/07IStBwc/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP was back in positive territory on Friday, registering an increase of 3% and moving to $2.34. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment registered a substantial increase on Saturday as XRP surged over 10%, moving beyond the $2.50 resistance level and settling at $2.57. However, it lost momentum on Sunday, dropping almost 3% to end the weekend at $2.50. Early selling pressure pushed XRP to an intraday low of $2.33 on Monday. It recovered from this level to register an increase of almost 1% and settle at $2.52. The current session sees XRP marginally up as buyers look to push towards $2.80 and $3.\par \par \uc2 Arbitrum (ARB) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Arbitrum (ARB) has been trading in a downward trajectory since losing momentum after reaching an intraday high of $0.956. As a result, ARB dropped nearly 11% on Tuesday, slipping below the 50-day SMA and settling at $0.82. ARB slipped below a key support level on Wednesday, dropping just over 4% to go below the 20-day SMA and settle at $0.787. Selling pressure intensified on Thursday as ARB fell almost 6% to $0.743.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/A0DAvB2H/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Buyers attempted a recovery on Friday as ARB rose to an intraday high of $0.774. However, it lost momentum after reaching this level and settled at $0.747, ultimately registering only a marginal increase. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment returned over the weekend as ARB dropped 0.55% on Saturday and nearly 2% on Sunday, settling at $0.730. The current week began with ARB remaining in the red, falling almost 4% to $0.702. ARB is up just over 1% during the ongoing session, rebounding from the $0.70 support level.\par \par \uc2 Filecoin (FIL) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Filecoin (FIL) slipped below a key support level on Monday as its recent \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trajectory continues. FIL slipped below the 50-day SMA on Tuesday after registering a drop of almost 11% and settling at $5.35. The price continued to drop on Wednesday, falling over 4% to go below the 20-day SMA and settle at $5.11. FIl attempted a recovery on Thursday but could not go past the 20-day SMA. Sellers ultimately retook control and pushed the price down 1.40% to $5.04. FIL recovered on Friday, rising over 3% to $5.21. Despite the positive momentum, FIL could not go past the 20-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/BX1ElA8D/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Sellers returned to the market over the weekend as FIL registered a marginal drop on Saturday and a drop of 2.20% on Sunday to settle at $5.08. Selling pressure intensified on Monday as FIL slipped below $5 and settled at $4.92, but not before settling at $4.63. The current session sees FIL up almost 3% as buyers look to keep the price above $5. FIL is presently trading around the $5.05 level.\par \par \uc2 Injective (INJ) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Injective (INJ) has been \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the previous week, dropping over 8% on Tuesday after failing to move beyond the 50-day SMA. Sellers retained control on Wednesday as INJ fell by 8.11% to go below the 20 and 200-day SMAs and settle at $21.88. The price continued to drop on Thursday, dropping almost 4% and settling at $21.07. Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pressure, INJ recovered on Friday, rising by 2.40% to $21.58. However, it could not go past the moving averages and was back in the red on Saturday, dropping just over 1% to $21.34.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/EZtVZfQU/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 INJ continued to decline on Sunday, dropping below $21 after declining 2.45% and settling at $20.82. The price plummeted to an intraday low of $18.56 on Monday as selling pressure intensified. However, INJ recovered from this level to settle at $20.10, ultimately registering a drop of 3.44%. The current session sees INJ up over 3% as buyers look to push it towards the resistance at $22.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This article is provided for informational purposes only. It is not offered or intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, financial, or other advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020250115el1e00018\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Why is the crypto market up today?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Biraajmaan Tamuly \par \uc2 614 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 January 2025\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2025. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The crypto market remains optimistic in the lead-up to President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s official inauguration on Jan. 20.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvYTYzMzIzMGQtM2Y5YS00NzQ5LThiYWItMDE3YzRiOTQzNWEw.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why is the crypto market up today?}}}\par \par \uc2 The global crypto market cap remained above $3.5 trillion on Jan. 14 after rising by 2.3% over the past 24 hours. Bitcoin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 (BTC)}}}\uc2  led the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  revival after the crypto asset wicked down to $89,000 for the first time since Nov. 17 but it closed its daily candle at $94,485.\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE)}}}\uc2 , Cardano {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 (\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 )}}}\uc2 , and XRP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 (XRP)}}}\uc2  were the best performers among the top ten cryptocurrencies, with rises of 9.3%, 6.8%, and 6.2%, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  promises revolutionary crypto policies on day 1\par \par \uc2 The crypto markets rallied after it was announced that President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would potentially issue a series of executive orders on the first day back at the White House, with crypto policies rumored to be a \u8220\'20\'1Cclear priority.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cointelegraph {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/trump-first-day-crypto-executive-orders-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that the newly elected president is set to address important agendas, including \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  de-banking and revoking the unpopular accounting policy that requires banks holding crypto assets to count them as liabilities.\par \par \uc2 In December 2024, it was rumored that crypto industry representatives were advising Trump to establish new crypto policies within the first 100 days. The wider market expects crypto to be a key point of discussion on Jan. 20, which was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s political campaign in 2024 largely appeased crypto investors globally and in the US, promising a crypto-friendly regulatory framework. A landmark proposal for a Strategic Bitcoin Reserve steered optimism and tax incentives for businesses and investments, encouraging growth and innovation.\par \par \uc2 Michael Saylor\uc2 , the chairman of \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2 , also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/saylor/status/1878789738720805176"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that the organization completed another round of BTC purchases, adding 2,530 BTC worth $243 million. The current buy-in keeps \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 10-week streak of continuous BTC acquisition.\par \par \uc2 The business intelligence firm {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://saylortracker.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently holds}}}\uc2  over 450,000 BTC worth $43.3 billion at current value.\par \par \uc2 Following \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s blueprint, \uc2 Semler Scientific\uc2  also acquired 237 BTC for $23.3 million, adding to its tally of 2,321 Bitcoin amassed since May 2024.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/trump-first-day-crypto-executive-orders-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Related: Donald Trump could issue crypto executive orders on first day: Report}}}\par \par \uc2 TOTAL crypto market targets $10T, says analyst\par \par \uc2 From a technical perspective, the TOTAL crypto market chart has moved from one key resistance level to another over the past few years. Each time a resistance level has been crossed, it has been flipped into a support level, as illustrated in the chart.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/019464fa-88ca-75ef-9b08-8af1b582fb46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Bitcoin Price, Markets, Donald Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 TOTAL crypto market cap weekly chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 The total crypto market exhibited a break of structure (BOS) from its previous high of $3 trillion in November 2021, exactly three years later in November 2024.\par \par \uc2 After six weeks of price discovery, the TOTAL crypto market has retraced to its previous high of $3 trillion. As mentioned earlier, based on historical outcomes, the likelihood of the $3 trillion level being turned into support is high.\par \par \uc2 Jelle, an independent crypto analyst, shared a similar outlook on the market and said,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CATH Breakout + consolidation + sweep of the lows. The total cryptocurrency market cap looks ready for a face-melting rally! Send it to 10 trillion.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/how-long-will-the-bitcoin-consolidation-last"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Related: How long will Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price consolidation last?}}}\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvYTYzMzIzMGQtM2Y5YS00NzQ5LThiYWItMDE3YzRiOTQzNWEw.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020250114el1e000ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
