\par\par \b \uc2 Crypto Price Analysis 1-9 BITCOIN: BTC, ETHEREUM: ETH, SOLANA: SOL, CARDANO:  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , APTOS: APT, INTERNET COMPUTER: ICP, FILECOIN: FIL\b0\par\par\uc2 Amara Khatri \par \uc2 2,476 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 January 2025\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2025, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Slump Could Set Stage For Rally Near Trump Inauguration}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC Must Work On Crypto \b  \highlight22Regulation\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano (\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 ) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Aptos (APT) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Internet Computer (ICP) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Filecoin (FIL) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) continued to drop for a second day as it slipped below $95,000 on Wednesday, falling to a low of $92,911 before recovering and moving to its current level of $94,442. The flagship currency is down almost 3% over the past 24 hours, as the crypto market lost $320 billion. BTC\u8217\'20\'19s drop comes despite spot Bitcoin ETFs defying \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment and registered inflows of around $52 million.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Ethereum (ETH) showed resilience, dropping only around 1.50% despite registering a substantial drop on Tuesday. The world\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest cryptocurrency is trading around the $3,300 level. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/XRP-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ripple (XRP)}}}\uc2  was one of the few assets that defied the market\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trajectory as it registered a marginal increase, buoyed by its partnership with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/LINK-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chainlink (LINK)}}}\uc2 . With the crypto markets in the doldrums, its market cap has dropped almost 2% to $3.32 trillion.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Slump Could Set Stage For Rally Near Trump Inauguration\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2025/01/crypto-price-analysis-1-8-bitcoin-btc-ethereum-eth-solana-sol-injective-inj-dogwifhat-wif-chainlink-link-uniswap-uni"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)}}}\uc2  saw a substantial decline as it dropped below $95,000 after resilient US job figures sent risk assets spiraling. The US Labor Department\u8217\'20\'19s JOLTS report showed around 8.1 million job vacancies, significantly more than the anticipated 7.74 million. The numbers led to a risk-off atmosphere in the markets and sent bond yield upwards and a decline in risk assets like BTC. According to QCP BTC\u8217\'20\'19s decline stemmed from liquidations of around $206 million in an hour. The \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  also reached the traditional markets, with the S&P 500 and Nasdaq witnessing significant \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The response of the traditional markets highlights BTC\u8217\'20\'19s interconnectedness with the wider financial market, especially during economic uncertainty. Meanwhile, spot Bitcoin ETFs have registered a 94% decline, falling from $987 million to $52.9 million. However, \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s IBIT remained the exception, registering $596 million in investments and bucking the trend of outflows witnessed across all ETFs. Meanwhile, Ark and \uc2 21Shares\uc2  registered significant outflows, with over $210 million withdrawn from the ARKB Fund.\par \par \uc2 QCP also highlighted the upcoming Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) decision and the Non-Farm Payroll (NFP) data, which could substantially impact BTC\u8217\'20\'19s price. However, the firm also stated the recent decline could be temporary, and markets could see a substantial rally when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  takes office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith market anticipation building, we believe bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s pullback is merely a pause, setting the stage for a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration fuels optimism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 SEC Must Work On Crypto \b \highlight22\uc2 Regulation\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Gary Gensler\uc2 , the outgoing chair of the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) believes there is a lot of work to be done in regulating altcoins and intermediaries in the crypto market. Gensler stated that regular investors still don\u8217\'20\'19t receive adequate disclosures or information from \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  firms. Gensler\u8217\'20\'19s SEC tenure has been marked by enforcement action against several crypto players ranging from fraudsters to significant crypto names like \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and \uc2 DRW Holdings\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gensler announced he would step down as SEC Chair on January 20, when President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  takes office. Trump has nominated \uc2 Paul Atkins\uc2  as SEC Chair. Atkins is known for his pro-crypto views and is widely expected to tone down enforcement action against crypto firms and take a favorable view of the industry. Gensler pointed out that his predecessor, \uc2 Jay Clayton\uc2 , who led the agency during the first Trump administration, brought 80 crypto-related cases. The agency under Clayton cracked down on companies issuing tokens that were deemed securities. However, Gensler focused on market intermediaries flouting compliance with securities laws for registration and disclosure. Gensler also believes a majority of crypto projects will not survive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen a field that\u8217\'20\'19s so much wrapped up in sentiment and not so much about fundamentals.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/BTC-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)}}}\uc2  continued to slide as concerns about rising bond yields and the Federal Reserve monetary policy continued to mount. BTC went from a recent high of $102,668 to a low of $92,546 as macroeconomic factors turned against risk assets like BTC. The flagship currency plummeted over 5% on Tuesday and nearly 2% on Wednesday, slipping below key moving averages and support levels. If sellers continue to dominate, BTC could give up the gains since the beginning of January and drop to $90,000. BTC is down nearly 1% during the current session, hitting a low of $93,512.\par \par \uc2 BTC was \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the new year started, registering an increase of just over 1% on Wednesday (January 1) and settling at $94,376. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment increased substantially on Thursday as BTC surged past the 50-day SMA to an intraday high of $97,661. However, it could not stay at this level and ultimately settled at $96,882, registering an increase of 2.59%. BTC faced considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday as buyers and sellers struggled to establish control. As a result, the price dropped to an intraday low of $95,604 and rose to an intraday high of $98,832 before settling above the 20-day SMA at $97,878. Sellers retained control over the weekend as BTC registered marginal increases on Saturday and Sunday to settle at $98,309.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/Y5MP6czA/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC registered a surge in \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment on Monday as it went past $100,000 and settled at $102,228 after registering an increase of almost 4%. However, sentiment changed on Tuesday as the price plummeted over 5% to slip below $100,000 and the 50-day SMA to settle at $97,019. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment persisted on Wednesday as BTC fell below the 20-day SMA and dropped to an intraday low of $92,546. However, it recovered from this level to reclaim $95,000 and settle at $95,121, ultimately registering a drop of 1.96%. The current session sees BTC down by almost 1% as market sentiment continues to weigh down the price. Some analysts, like Katie Stockton, a top technical analyst at Fairland Strategies, have warned investors to brace for a potential double-digit drop in BTC prices, suggesting the asset has been massively overbought in its latest bull run. The analyst believes BTC will find support around $84,000, implying a drop of 13%.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/ETH-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH)}}}\uc2  has stemmed its recent decline during the current session as it attempts to rebound from the $3,300 level. ETH was quite \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the previous week but lost momentum after failing to stay above the resistance at $3,700. Despite registering a marginal drop on Tuesday (December 31), ETH started the new year positively, registering an increase of 0.69% on Wednesday. ETH continued to push higher on Thursday, rising by almost 3% and settling at $3,452. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment registered a substantial increase on Friday as ETH went above the 20 and 50-day SMAs and $3,500 to settle at $3,607, an increase of 4.51%.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/EZ3ZPNWZ/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH registered an increase of 1.37% on Saturday and moved to $3,657 as selling pressure began to spike. ETH lost momentum on Sunday as it dropped by 0.61% to $3,634 but recovered on Monday to register an increase of 1.46%, reaching an intraday high of $3,744 before settling at $3,687. Market sentiment changed on Tuesday as ETH plummeted over 8% to slip below the 20 and 50-day SMAs and settle at $3,381. Sellers retained control on Wednesday as the price dropped to an intraday low of $3,209 before settling at $3,327. The current session sees ETH marginally up as buyers and sellers struggle to establish control. If sellers take control, ETH could slip below $3,300 and drop towards $3,000. On the other hand, if buyers retain control, it could go above the 20-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  (SOL) has failed to reclaim $200 as sellers continue to lower the price during the ongoing session. SOL was relatively \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  until recent sessions but lost momentum after failing to move above the 50-day SMA. The price registered an increase of almost 3% on Wednesday and moved to $194, starting the new year positively. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment registered a substantial rise on Thursday as SOL surged over 7% to move past the 20-day SMA and $200 to settle at $208. Buyers retained control on Friday, helping SOL register an increase of almost 5% and move to $217.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/WqP7uGgf/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, with the 50-day SMA coming into play, SOL lost momentum over the weekend, dropping 0.56% on Saturday and 1.52% on Sunday to settle at $213. The current week began with SOL reaching an intraday high of $223 before settling at $218, an increase of 2.30%. However, it dropped substantially on Tuesday, falling by 7.38% and settling at $202. SOL slipped below $200 on Wednesday, falling to an intraday low of $188. However, it recovered from this level to go above the 20-day SMA and settle at $197. The current session sees SOL down almost 2%, slipping below the 20-day SMA and trading around $194.\par \par \uc2 Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/ADA-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano (\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 )}}}\uc2  registered a substantial jump on Wednesday as it started the new year on a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  note, registering an increase of 9% and settling at $0.92. Buyers retained control on Thursday as \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  went past the 20-day SMA, rising over 4% to $0.96. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment registered a substantial increase on Friday as \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged over 13% to go above the 50-day SMA and $1 to settle at $1.08. However, momentum waned on Saturday as \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped by 1.56% to $1.07. The price recovered on Sunday, rising almost 2% and settling at $1.09.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/aTXEUv7f/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The current week began with \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  experiencing \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  as buyers and sellers struggled to establish control. \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  ultimately registered a marginal increase before registering a substantial drop of over 9% on Tuesday to slip below the 50-day SMA and $1 to settle at $0.99. Sellers retained control on Wednesday as \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  faced significant \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ultimately registering a drop of over 4% and settling at $0.94. The current session sees \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  down by almost 2%, trading around $0.92, having slipped below the 20-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 Aptos (APT) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Aptos (APT) rebounded from a low of $8.41 on Wednesday to register an increase of 3.48% and move above $9 to settle at $9.01. Buyers retained control on Thursday as APT rose almost 3% to $9.27. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment registered a substantial increase on Friday as APT registered a rise of 5.48% to move past a key resistance level and settle at $9.78. APT remained positive over the weekend, registering an increase of 2.14% on Saturday and 1% on Sunday to go above the 20-day SMA and $1 and settle at $10.09.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/v6tuvCMe/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The current week began with APT facing considerable selling pressure as it fell to an intraday low of $9.81. However, it recovered from this level to register an increase of 0.85% and settle at $10.17. Sentiment changed on Tuesday as markets turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As a result, APT dropped over 5% to slip below $10 and settled at $9.65. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified on Wednesday as APT slipped below the 20-day SMA and fell to an intraday low of $8.64 before settling at $9.01, a drop of almost 7%. The current session sees APT down just over 2% and trading around $8.82 as sellers look to drive it below the 200-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 Internet Computer (ICP) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Recent \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment has seen Internet Computer (ICP) slip below $11 as sellers continue to dominate the markets. Despite ending 2024 in the red, ICP started the year positively, registering an increase of over 6% on Wednesday to go above $10 and settle at $10.48. ICP continued to go higher on Thursday, rising by 1.81% to $10.67. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified substantially on Friday as ICP surged over 16% to go above the 20 and 50-day SMAs and settle at $12.40. However, it lost momentum after reaching this level, dropping 0.81% on Saturday and 1.46% on Sunday to end the weekend at $12.12.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/Jc6aBqyN/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The current week began with ICP witnessing considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  as buyers and sellers struggled to establish control. As a result, ICP rose to an intraday high of $12.52 and fell to an intraday low of $11.83 before ultimately settling at $12.21. However, market sentiment changed on Tuesday as ICP dropped almost 10% to slip below the 50-day SMA and settle at $11.02. Sellers retained control on Wednesday as ICP fell to an intraday low of $10.37, briefly going below the 20-day SMA before recovering and settling at $10.87. The current session sees ICP down almost 4% as sellers look to drive it below $10.\par \par \uc2 Filecoin (FIL) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Filecoin (FIL) has registered a sharp drop over the past few sessions and has almost given up all of its gains since the beginning of the year. FIL registered an increase of over 3% on Wednesday to go above $5 and settle at $5.10. The price continued to push higher on Thursday, increasing just over 4% to $5.30. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment picked up on Friday as FIL rose almost 7% to move above the 20-day SMA and settle at $5.66. The price faced a marginal wobble on Saturday but recovered on Sunday to go above the 50-day SMA after an increase of almost 5% and settle at $5.91\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/LWgZ3JRF/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Buyers retained control on Monday as FIL surged to an intraday high of $6.29. However, it could not stay at this level and dropped to $5.99, ultimately registering an increase of 1.20%. FIL registered a significant decline on Tuesday as markets turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dropping almost 11% to go below the 50-day SMA and settle at $5.35. Sellers retained control on Wednesday as FIL slipped below the 20-day SMA and settled at $5.11. The current session sees FIL down just over 2% as buyers look to drive it below $5.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This article is provided for informational purposes only. It is not offered or intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, financial, or other advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020250110el190000s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
