\par\par \b \uc2 Crypto Price Analysis 1-8 BITCOIN: BTC, ETHEREUM: ETH, SOLANA: SOL, INJECTIVE: INJ, DOGWIFHAT: WIF, CHAINLINK: LINK, UNISWAP: UNI\b0\par\par\uc2 Amara Khatri \par \uc2 2,564 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 January 2025\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2025, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Plummets Below $97,000}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A Surge In Liquidations}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US CFTC Chair To Step Down}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Injective (INJ) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogwifhat (WIF) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chainlink (LINK) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) plummeted below $100,000 as the crypto markets witnessed a significant drop on Tuesday, driven by stronger-than-anticipated economic indicators that could delay Federal Reserve rate cuts. BTC was trading above $100,000 since January 6, when it reached an intraday high of $102,464. However, its decline saw the price plummet below $100,000 to its current $96,278. The price is down almost 6% over the past 24 hours, with sellers firmly in control.\par \par \uc2 The rest of the crypto market fared no better, with Ethereum (ETH) plummeting over 9% to slip below $3,500. \uc2 Solana\uc2  (SOL) also dipped below $200 after shedding over 9% and is currently trading around $197. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/DOGE-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE)}}}\uc2  plummeted almost 10% and slipped to $0.352. Ripple (XRP), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/ADA-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano (\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 )}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/TRX-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tron (TRX)}}}\uc2 , Chainlink (LINK), Toncoin (TON), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/XLM-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stellar (XLM)}}}\uc2 , Hedera (HBAR), Polkadot (DOT), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/LTC-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Litecoin (LTC)}}}\uc2 , Uniswap (UNI) and other altcoins also registered substantial losses.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Plummets Below $97,000\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2025/01/crypto-price-analysis-1-7-bitcoin-btc-ethereum-eth-solana-sol-algorand-algo-hedera-hbar-near-protocol-near-arbitrum-arb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)}}}\uc2  registered a shard drop on Tuesday to slip below $100,000 after stronger-than-expected economic indicators put pressure on risk assets like crypto. According to data from \uc2 Coin Metrics\uc2 , the flagship currency fell to a low of $96,525, dropping over 5%. Crypto stocks, including \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2 , \uc2 Mara Holdings\uc2 , \uc2 Core Scientific\uc2 , and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  also registered substantial drops. The decline comes after a sudden increase in the 10-year \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  Yield following data released by the \uc2 Institute for Supply Management\uc2  showed faster-than-expected growth in the US service sector, adding to concerns about inflation.\par \par \uc2 Market watchers expect BTC to reach $200,000 this year, with investors hopeful a clear regulatory framework will support \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices and benefit crypto stocks. However, the uncertainty surrounding rate cuts by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  could adversely impact crypto prices. The Fed signaled it would make fewer rate cuts in 2025, a decision that rattled markets.\par \par \uc2 A Surge In Liquidations\par \par \uc2 The cryptocurrency market saw a surge in liquidations after Bitcoin (BTC)\u8217\'20\'19s unexpected drop below $100,000. Data from Coinglass showed that over $200 million in long positions were liquidated in an hour. A total of $483 million in long positions was liquidated in 24 hours. Other altcoins, including Ethereum (ETH) and Solana (SOL), also registered substantial drops, with ETH slipping below the crucial $3,500 level and SOL dropping below $200. While lower than the single largest 24-hour or hourly liquidations seen in December/January, the numbers are still significant, with over 129,900 traders liquidated in the past 24 hours. The largest liquidation was seen on \uc2 Binance\uc2 , with nearly $12 million liquidated.\par \par \uc2 US CFTC Chair To Step Down\par \par \uc2 Rostin Behnam\uc2 , the Chair of the \uc2 Commodity Futures Trading Commission\uc2  (CFTC), will step down on January 20, signaling the end of a four-year tenure that saw significant enforcement action in the crypto sector and calls for stronger regulations. Behnam oversaw several high-profile cases, including a $4.3 billion settlement with \uc2 Binance\uc2 . However, he expressed concern about the lack of oversight in the \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  space, describing current regulations as insufficient.\par \par \uc2 Under Behnam, the CFTC finalized Federal guidelines for carbon offset trading and expanded oversight into digital assets. He also ensured action against \uc2 Binance\uc2  for operating illegally in the US as an unlicensed crypto derivatives platform and failing to comply with regulations. He also flagged regulatory gaps in the crypto markets, arguing many tokens qualify as commodities and should come under the CFTC\u8217\'20\'19s jurisdiction, calling upon his replacement to deliver \u8220\'20\'1Crenewed focus\u8221\'20\'1D for more clarity.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Brian Quintenz, a former CFTC commissioner and the current head of policy at \uc2 Andreessen Horowitz\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s crypto division, has emerged as the top pick to replace Behnam.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/BTC-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)}}}\uc2  has plummeted below $100,000 after dropping over 5% on Tuesday as markets turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  after stronger-than-expected economic indicators put significant pressure on risk assets. BTC slumped to a low of $96,202 on Tuesday, erasing a significant portion of the gains made the previous week before rising slightly to settle at $97,019. Meanwhile, \uc2 Katie Stockton\uc2 , a top technical analyst at Fairland Strategies, has warned investors to brace for a potential double-digit drop in BTC prices, suggesting the asset has been massively overbought in its latest bull run. The analyst believes BTC will find support around $84,000, implying a drop of 13%. A secondary support at around $73,800 will come into play in the event of a steeper selloff.\par \par \uc2 Stockton said in a note to clients she foresaw near-term weakness despite BTC reclaiming the $100,000 level, adding that BTC could slip below $90,000 to find support around the $84,000 mark. Despite her prediction, Stockton remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  about BTC's long-term prospects, pointing to a strong long-term backdrop that could support the asset.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBitcoin has a rebound underway, but we expect it to fade quickly, yielding a lower high relative to the December peak. The weekly stochastics have an active overbought downturn, and the daily stochastics are newly overbought, so we think further upside will be limited in the near term.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 BTC had been quite \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite dropping to a low of $91,279 last Monday. It recovered from this level on Tuesday and surged to an intraday high of 496,159. However, buyers lost momentum after reaching this level, and BTC ultimately settled at $93,383, registering an increase of almost 1%. The price continued to push higher on Wednesday, rising 1.06% to $94,373. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified considerably on Thursday as BTC registered an increase of almost 3% to go above $95,000 and settle at 496,823. The price pushed above the 20 and 50-day SMAs on Friday after rising 1.09% and settling at $97,878.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/G5IATjzH/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The weekend saw buyers retain control as BTC registered a marginal increase on Saturday and Sunday to settle at $98,312. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified substantially on Monday as BTC surged past $100,000 and settled at $102,228. However, \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment returned on Tuesday following stronger-than-expected economic indicators putting pressure on risk assets. As a result, BTC plummeted over 5% to go below $100,000 and the 50-day SMA and settled at $97,019. The current session sees BTC marginally down as sellers look to drive BTC below the 20-day SMA. If sellers retain control and the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment persists, BTC could drop to $90,000. If Stockton\u8217\'20\'19s prediction holds, BTC could slip below $90,000.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/ETH-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH)}}}\uc2  is struggling to remain above $3,300 as \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment in the market drives prices lower. ETH lost the crucial $3,500 level on Tuesday after plummeting over 8%, slipping below key moving averages. ETH was quite \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  the previous week despite facing considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  and registering only a marginal increase on Monday. Buyers attempted a move towards $3,500 on Tuesday as ETH reached an intraday high of $3,448. However, it could not go any further as sellers drove the price down almost 1% to $3,333. Sentiment changed on Wednesday as ETH registered an increase of 0.69% and settled at $3,356. Buyers retained control on Thursday as ETH rose almost 3% and settled at $3,452.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/3Cqhsn6w/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment registered a substantial increase on Friday as ETH went above the 20 and 50-day SMAs and $3,500 to settle at $3,607. The weekend began with ETH rising by 1.37% on Saturday and moving to $3,657. However, with the resistance at $3,700 coming into play, the price dipped by 0.615% to settle at $3,634. Buyers attempted to clear $3,700 on Monday as ETH rose to an intraday high of $3,744. However, ETH lost momentum after reaching this level and ultimately settled at $3,687. Markets turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, and ETH plummeted over 8% to slip below the 20 and 50-day SMAs and the crucial $3,500 level to $3,381. ETH remains in the red during the current session, with the price down almost 2%, as sellers look to drive it below $3,300.\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  (SOL) has registered a substantial drop over the past two sessions as markets turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the release of economic data. SOL started the previous week experiencing significant \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  as buyers and sellers struggled to establish control. Buyers ultimately gained the upper hand as the price registered an increase of 0.72% and moved to $191. SOL surged to an intraday high of $199 on Tuesday as buyers attempted to push above $200. However, they lost momentum at this point, allowing sellers to take control and drive SOL down to $189. Buyers returned to the market on Wednesday as SOL registered an increase of almost 3% and moved to $194. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified significantly on Thursday as SOL surged past the 20-day SMA and $200 to settle at $208.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/bAvu3JqO/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL registered an increase of almost 5% on Friday, rising to $217 as buyers set their sights on $220. However, with sellers active at this level, SOL lost momentum on Saturday, dropping marginally to $216. Sellers retained control on Sunday, falling by 1.52% as SOL ended the weekend in the red at $213. The price recovered on Monday as SOL reached an intraday high of $223. SOL could not remain at this level and ultimately fell to $218, registering an increase of 2.30%. SOL plummeted 7% on Tuesday as markets turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  and settled at $202. The current session sees SOL below $200 and the 20-day SMA, with the price down over 4% and trading around $193.\par \par \uc2 Injective (INJ) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Injective (INJ) was extremely \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week before dropping significantly on Tuesday after failing to move past the 50-day SMA. Despite dropping to a low of $19.49 last Tuesday, INJ made a strong recovery on Wednesday, registering an increase of almost 5% and moving to $20.52. The price continued to push higher on Thursday, rising by 5.76% and settling at $21.70. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified on Friday as INJ went past the 20 and 200-day SMAs after registering an increase of over 6% and settling at $23.03.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/C0WBGK3O/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Buyers retained control on Saturday as INJ registered an increase of 2.41% and moved to $23.59. Sellers attempted to take control on Sunday as INJ dipped to an intraday low of $22.68. However, it recovered from this level to register an increase of 7.65% and ended the weekend at $25.39. INJ experienced considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday as buyers and sellers attempted to establish control. Buyers ultimately gained the upper hand as INJ registered an increase of just over 2% and settled at $25.91. However, \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment returned on Tuesday as the price plummeted over 8% and settled at $23.80. The current session sees sellers remain in control, with INJ down almost 5% and trading at $22.72.\par \par \uc2 Dogwifhat (WIF) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Dogwifhat (WIF) has been trading in the red since the weekend after failing to move above the 200-day SMA on Saturday. WIF had been trading in a narrow range since December 20, when it dropped to an intraday low of $1.72. It broke out of this range towards the end of last week, registering a substantial jump of almost 9% on Thursday to go above $2 and settle at $2.02. Buyers retained control on Friday as WIF rose over 7% to go above the 20-day SMA and settle at $2.16. However, sentiment waned on Saturday, with the 200-day SMA acting as a dynamic resistance level. As a result, WIF could only register a marginal increase and settle at $2.17.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/VnDu6f3Z/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 With buyers losing momentum, sellers took control on Sunday, driving WIF down by 3.51% to $2.10. WIF experienced a marginal decline on Monday, falling to $2.08. However, \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified considerably on Tuesday as the price plummeted below the 20-day SMA, dropping over 11% and settling at $1.85. The current session sees WIF marginally down as sellers look to drive the price lower.\par \par \uc2 Chainlink (LINK) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/LINK-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chainlink (LINK)}}}\uc2  slipped below the 50-day SMA on Monday (December 30), dropping almost 2% to $20.57. Sellers retained control on Tuesday as the price fell below the $20 support level and settled at $19.99. However, LINK recovered from this level on Wednesday to register an increase of 8.55% to reclaim $20 and go above the 50-day SMA to settle at $21.70. Buyers retained control on Thursday as LINK rose by 1.64% and settled at $22.05. Friday saw an increase of 6.39% as LINK moved to $23.46.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/quAfNWfK/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK faced substantial \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Saturday before registering a marginal increase and settling at $23.59. The price registered a marginal drop on Sunday, falling to $23.56 and ending the weekend in the red. Buyers attempted a push above $25 on Monday as LINK rose to an intraday high of $24.76. However, they lost momentum after reaching this level, and LINK ultimately settled at $23.83. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment returned to the market on Tuesday as LINK fell over 10%, slipping below the 20 and 50-day SMAs and settling at $21.38. The current session sees sellers retain control, with LINK down over 2% and trading around $20.89.\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) stalled around the $15.50 mark as buyers lost momentum, allowing sellers to drive the price below $15. UNI was quite \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  the previous week, rising almost 3% on Wednesday to go above the 50-day SMA and settle at $13.62. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified considerably on Thursday as UNI registered an increase of 5.52% to go above the 20-day SMA and settle at $14.37. Buyers retained control on Friday, pushing UNI up by almost 6% to $15.18. Sellers attempted to drive UNI towards the 20-day SMA on Saturday as the price fell to an intraday low of $14.76. However, UNI recovered to register a marginal increase and ended the day at $15.28.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/QhJDwzcM/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 With sellers active around $15.50, UNI lost momentum on Sunday, registering a drop of 0.79% and settling at $15.16. The current week began with sellers retaining control as UNI dropped marginally to $15.08. Selling pressure intensified substantially on Wednesday as UNI plummeted over 10% to go below the 20 and 50-day SMAs and $15 to settle at $13.54. Sellers are attempting to drive UNI below $13 during the current session, with the price down 1.30% and trading around $13.26.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This article is provided for informational purposes only. It is not offered or intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, financial, or other advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020250109el1800016\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 1/8: BTC, ETH, XRP, BNB, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , DOGE,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 AVAX\uc2 , SUI, LINK\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,871 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 January 2025\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2025. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and altcoins have corrected sharply, signaling that the bears continue to sell on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjUtMDEvMDE5NDQ2YzAtNjJhZi03ZjhhLWE5NGItODcwNTIzOGQ4YmIy.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 1/8: BTC, ETH, XRP, BNB, SOL, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, SUI, LINK}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has pulled back near $95,000, indicating that the bears are trying to strengthen their position. A minor advantage in favor of the bulls is that the US spot Bitcoin exchange-traded funds witnessed inflows of $52.4 million on Jan. 7, even when Bitcoin fell more than 5%, per Farside Investors {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://farside.co.uk/btc/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2 . This suggests that investors are not dumping their positions as they expect the bull run to resume.\par \par \uc2 BitMEX co-founder \uc2 Arthur Hayes\uc2  said in a blog post that the addition of up to $612 billion in new liquidity in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-fed-money-printing-bitcoin-rally-q1-2025-hayes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first quarter of 2025 could benefit Bitcoin}}}\uc2 . That could counterbalance any delays in implementing the \u8220\'20\'1Cproposed pro-crypto and pro-business legislation\u8221\'20\'1D by President-elect Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/019446b6-4921-7b98-8aa3-305e69b5df75"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin, Cryptocurrencies, Bitcoin Price, BitMEX, XRP, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Cardano, Price Analysis, Binance Coin, Chainlink, Market Analysis, Ether Price, Solana, Avalanche, Bitcoin ETF, ETF, SUI}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto market data daily view. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Along with Bitcoin, analysts are also turning positive on Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ). Derive head of research Dr. Sean Dawson told Cointelegraph that a regulatory-friendly environment and successful Pectra update could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ether-price-surge-donald-trump-pectra-upgrade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 propel Ether to $12,000}}}\uc2  by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 What are the crucial support levels to watch out for in Bitcoin and altcoins? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s failure to maintain above $100,000 could have tempted short-term buyers to book profits. That pulled the price below the moving averages on Jan. 7.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/019446b8-534d-751a-bc00-8b114355be37"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin, Cryptocurrencies, Bitcoin Price, BitMEX, XRP, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Cardano, Price Analysis, Binance Coin, Chainlink, Market Analysis, Ether Price, Solana, Avalanche, Bitcoin ETF, ETF, SUI}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 Both moving averages are flattening out, and the relative strength index (\uc2 RSI\uc2 ) is just below the midpoint, indicating that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum is weakening. The BTC/USDT pair could descend to $90,000, which is likely to act as a solid support. Sellers will have to yank the price below the $90,000 to $85,000 support zone to signal a short-term trend reversal.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns up from the current level and breaks above the moving averages, it will indicate that every minor dip is being purchased. That will improve the prospects of a rally above $102,725. If that happens, the pair may retest the all-time high of $108,353.\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 Ether turned down and fell below the breakout level of $3,555 on Jan. 7, suggesting that the breakout from the ascending triangle pattern on Jan. 3 was a bull trap.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/019446b8-f311-7388-b787-54a298bf580a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin, Cryptocurrencies, Bitcoin Price, BitMEX, XRP, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Cardano, Price Analysis, Binance Coin, Chainlink, Market Analysis, Ether Price, Solana, Avalanche, Bitcoin ETF, ETF, SUI}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 Sellers have pulled the price below the uptrend line, invalidating the triangle pattern. The failure of the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup is a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sign. The ETH/USDT pair could descend to $3,102 and then to $3,000. Buyers are expected to aggressively defend the $3,000 to $2,850 zone.\par \par \uc2 Any recovery is expected to face selling at the moving averages. The bulls will have to pierce the 50-day simple moving average ($3,576) to signal a comeback. The pair could rise to $3,745 and later to $4,094.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 Buyers failed to push XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) above the resistance line, indicating that the price may remain inside the triangle for some more time.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/019446b9-8e4d-78db-b5ae-5c12f44c5695"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin, Cryptocurrencies, Bitcoin Price, BitMEX, XRP, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Cardano, Price Analysis, Binance Coin, Chainlink, Market Analysis, Ether Price, Solana, Avalanche, Bitcoin ETF, ETF, SUI}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price skids below the 20-day exponential moving average ($2.28), the XRP/USDT pair could fall to the support line. A break and close below the triangle will signal that the pair may have topped out in the short term. That could start a pullback to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $1.90 and subsequently to $1.62.\par \par \uc2 The trend will favor the buyers if they push and sustain the price above the resistance line. The pair could climb to $2.73 and, after that, to $2.91.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 BNB\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) tight-range trading resolved to the upside with a close above $722 on Jan. 6, but the bulls could not sustain the higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/019446ba-13d0-722c-90d3-1d31afd705fc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin, Cryptocurrencies, Bitcoin Price, BitMEX, XRP, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Cardano, Price Analysis, Binance Coin, Chainlink, Market Analysis, Ether Price, Solana, Avalanche, Bitcoin ETF, ETF, SUI}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price turned down sharply on Jan. 7, trapping the aggressive bulls. There is minor support at the 50-day SMA ($688), but the level is likely to be broken. The BNB/USDT pair may then tumble to the solid support at $635.\par \par \uc2 Time is running out for the bulls. If they want to retain control, buyers will have to swiftly thrust the price above $745. That could clear the path for a potential rally to $794, which is expected to act as a strong resistance.\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  price analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) recovery could not sustain above the 50-day SMA ($217), indicating that bears are active at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/019446ba-a5e5-7615-9532-97b4665c7087"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin, Cryptocurrencies, Bitcoin Price, BitMEX, XRP, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Cardano, Price Analysis, Binance Coin, Chainlink, Market Analysis, Ether Price, Solana, Avalanche, Bitcoin ETF, ETF, SUI}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price turned down sharply on Jan. 7 and plunged below the moving averages. That opened the doors for a fall to the crucial support at the uptrend line. If bears sink the price below the uptrend line, the \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT pair could fall to $175 and later to $165.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the price rebounds off the uptrend line, it will signal that the bulls are fiercely defending the level. The bulls will then try to push the price above the 20-day EMA ($204). Buyers will be back in command on a break and close above $223.\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) failure to break above the $0.40 resistance may have attracted profit booking by short-term buyers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/019446bb-341d-7561-be40-c60f7c120c08"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin, Cryptocurrencies, Bitcoin Price, BitMEX, XRP, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Cardano, Price Analysis, Binance Coin, Chainlink, Market Analysis, Ether Price, Solana, Avalanche, Bitcoin ETF, ETF, SUI}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 The DOGE/USDT pair turned down sharply and broke below the moving averages on Jan. 7. If the price maintains below the 20-day EMA ($0.35), it will increase the likelihood of a range-bound action between $0.30 and $0.40 for a while. The flattish moving averages and the RSI near the midpoint do not give a clear advantage either to the bulls or the bears.\par \par \uc2 Buyers will have to push and sustain the price above $0.40 to set up a retest of $0.48. On the downside, a break below $0.30 could sink the pair to $0.23.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) rose above the $1.12 resistance on Jan. 7, but the breakout turned out to be a bull trap.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/019446bb-ca41-7622-af43-e7c445b73502"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin, Cryptocurrencies, Bitcoin Price, BitMEX, XRP, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Cardano, Price Analysis, Binance Coin, Chainlink, Market Analysis, Ether Price, Solana, Avalanche, Bitcoin ETF, ETF, SUI}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price turned down sharply and fell to the 20-day EMA ($0.98). If the 20-day EMA cracks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could drop to the solid support at $0.80. A bounce off $0.80 will increase the possibility of a range formation. The pair may oscillate between $0.80 and $1.18 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 Buyers will have to drive and maintain the price above $1.18 to be back in the driver\u8217\'20\'19s seat. The pair may then climb to $1.33.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-is-xrp-price-down-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why is XRP price down today?}}}\par \par \uc2 Avalanche price analysis\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) closed above the 50-day SMA ($43.38) on Jan. 6, but the bulls could not maintain the breakout.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/019446bc-ce19-7cfe-81f1-987d32cc4246"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin, Cryptocurrencies, Bitcoin Price, BitMEX, XRP, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Cardano, Price Analysis, Binance Coin, Chainlink, Market Analysis, Ether Price, Solana, Avalanche, Bitcoin ETF, ETF, SUI}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price turned down sharply on Jan. 7 and fell below the moving averages, indicating aggressive selling by the bears on rallies. Sellers will try to sink the AVAX/USDT pair to the strong support zone between $35 and $33.60.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the support zone and rises above the 20-day EMA ($40.53), the pair may consolidate between $33.60 and $45 for a while. Contrarily, a break below $33.60 could sink the pair to $30.\par \par \uc2 Sui price analysis\par \par \uc2 Sui ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/sui-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SUI}}}\uc2  ) is correcting in an uptrend. The price has reached the 20-day EMA ($4.58), an essential near-term support to watch out for.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/019446bd-4fdc-796b-ae37-614efc470b52"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin, Cryptocurrencies, Bitcoin Price, BitMEX, XRP, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Cardano, Price Analysis, Binance Coin, Chainlink, Market Analysis, Ether Price, Solana, Avalanche, Bitcoin ETF, ETF, SUI}}}\par \par \uc2 SUI/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA with strength, it will signal that buyers remain in control. The bulls will then try to resume the uptrend by pushing the price above the overhead resistance at $5.36.\par \par \uc2 Instead, if the price breaks below the 20-day EMA, the SUI/USDT pair may slump to the 50-day SMA ($4.16). Sellers will have to tug the price below the 50-day SMA to seize control. That could start a decline to $3.50.\par \par \uc2 Chainlink price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bears dragged Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/chainlink-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) below the moving averages on Jan. 7, indicating selling at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/019446be-0add-75bf-b550-be5996b5a37a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin, Cryptocurrencies, Bitcoin Price, BitMEX, XRP, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Cardano, Price Analysis, Binance Coin, Chainlink, Market Analysis, Ether Price, Solana, Avalanche, Bitcoin ETF, ETF, SUI}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 The LINK/USDT pair could fall to the neckline of the H&S pattern at $20, where the buyers are expected to mount a strong defense. If the price rebounds off $20 and rises above the moving averages, it will point to a possible consolidation in the short term. The pair may swing between $20 and $26 for some time.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, a break and close below $20 will complete the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup, paving the way for further declines. The pair may tumble to $16 and subsequently to $14.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjUtMDEvMDE5NDQ2YzAtNjJhZi03ZjhhLWE5NGItODcwNTIzOGQ4YmIy.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020250108el18000ba\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Why is the crypto market down today?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Nancy Lubale \par \uc2 950 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 January 2025\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2025. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Cascading derivatives liquidations and risk-off mode following two stronger-than-expected US economic data prints appear to be factors in the current crypto market sell-off.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvODAzMjgxMmQtMWQ1MC00NmFiLWI5NjUtYTBjYjZkZDQxYTYz.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why is the crypto market down today?}}}\par \par \uc2 The cryptocurrency market took a hit today, with the total market capitalization dropping by around 6.3% to about $3.35 trillion on Jan. 8 as strong US economic data pointed toward potential interest rate hikes.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/0194450a-1ae5-7b9c-a226-ba80d8e6f067"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Federal Reserve, Central Bank, Bitcoin Price, Bitcoin \b  \highlight22Regulation\b0 \highlight22 , Economy, Markets, Stocks, Inflation, Interest Rate, Binance, Stablecoin}}}\par \par \uc2 24-hour performance of large-cap cryptocurrencies. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s look closer at the factors driving the crypto market down today.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin leads the market slump\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s crypto market decline is part of a correction that started during the early New York trading hours on Jan. 7 when Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) lost the $100,000 level, as two stronger-than-expected US economic data prints quelled the early-year momentum by crypto assets.\par \par \uc2 BTC price dropped as much as 6.35% to an intra-day low of $05,279 on Jan. 8. The decline in the pioneer cryptocurrency triggered panic selling among crypto investors, with prices dropping across the board.\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) lost all the gains made over the last seven days, dipping as low as $3,300 on Jan. 8, recording 10% losses over the last 24 hours.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/0194450a-8a54-7a11-be30-d0deb68427ff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Federal Reserve, Central Bank, Bitcoin Price, Bitcoin \b  \highlight22Regulation\b0 \highlight22 , Economy, Markets, Stocks, Inflation, Interest Rate, Binance, Stablecoin}}}\par \par \uc2 Performance of top 10 largest cryptocurrencies by market cap. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CoinMarketCap}}}\par \par \uc2 Other top-cap cryptocurrencies posting significant losses on Dec. 16 are Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), which are down 12%, 11.7% and 10%, respectively.\par \par \uc2 The sharp decline in prices liquidated nearly $631 million long positions across derivatives markets betting on rising prices, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.coinglass.com/LiquidationData"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CoinGlass}}}\uc2 , marking the first large leverage flush of the year. Long BTC leveraged positions totaling $111 million were liquidated on the day.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/0194450a-e56e-7a21-8893-4d25a2d2e642"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Federal Reserve, Central Bank, Bitcoin Price, Bitcoin \b  \highlight22Regulation\b0 \highlight22 , Economy, Markets, Stocks, Inflation, Interest Rate, Binance, Stablecoin}}}\par \par \uc2 Total crypto liquidations. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.coinglass.com/LiquidationData"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CoinGlass}}}\par \par \uc2 A similar move was seen on Dec. 18 in the derivatives market when more than $844 million long positions were liquidated. These liquidations accompany a 12% drop in TOTAL\u8212\'20\'14the combined market capitalization of all cryptocurrencies\u8212\'20\'14with more than $1.2 billion being wiped off the crypto market.\par \par \uc2 A predominance of long liquidations suggests that the crypto market was overleveraged on the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  side, primarily due to profit-taking and risk-off mode {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-4-us-jolts-data-bitcoin-trader-92k-dip"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 following strong US economic data}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Strong US economic data triggers risk-off mode\par \par \uc2 The ongoing correction in the crypto market mirrors the weakness witnessed in US equities. The S&P 500 dropped by 1.1% to close the day at 5,509.03 on Jan. 7, while the Nasdaq composite index declined by 375 points.\par \par \uc2 The Dow Jones index clocked its second consecutive daily loss, dropping 0.61% to close the trading day on Jan. 7 at 42,528.36.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe S&P 500 is now down 75 points today and has erased its year-to-date gain,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KobeissiLetter/status/1876728313860816970"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  capital markets commentator The Kobeissi Letter in response to the market\u8217\'20\'19s reaction to the economic data prints.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver $625 billion of market cap has been erased from the stock market today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/0194450c-13e2-7161-8a2c-9bb492502f76"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Federal Reserve, Central Bank, Bitcoin Price, Bitcoin \b  \highlight22Regulation\b0 \highlight22 , Economy, Markets, Stocks, Inflation, Interest Rate, Binance, Stablecoin}}}\par \par \uc2 24-hour performance of US equities Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finviz.com/map.ashx?t=sec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Financial Visualizations}}}\par \par \uc2 The strong data also has investors further lowering their expectations of rate cuts by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  in 2025. This impacts \b \highlight22\uc2 investor sentiment\b0 \highlight\uc2  toward riskier assets like cryptocurrencies.\par \par \uc2 Market participants now see just a 95% chance of interest rates remaining the same at the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s Jan. 29 meeting, up from 90.4% just a week ago and 62.7% over a month ago, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cmegroup.com/markets/interest-rates/cme-fedwatch-tool.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the CME FedWatch tool}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/0194450c-8ec1-777e-9f23-2b301fcf184e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Federal Reserve, Central Bank, Bitcoin Price, Bitcoin \b  \highlight22Regulation\b0 \highlight22 , Economy, Markets, Stocks, Inflation, Interest Rate, Binance, Stablecoin}}}\par \par \uc2 Fed target rate probabilities for Jan. 29 FOMC meeting. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cmegroup.com/markets/interest-rates/cme-fedwatch-tool.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CME Group}}}\par \par \uc2 Zooming out even further, the odds of rate cuts in March and May are below 50% at 37% and 42%, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Crypto market flips 50 SMA into resistance\par \par \uc2 The latest drawdown in crypto prices has seen TOTAL\u8212\'20\'14the combined market capitalization of all cryptocurrencies\u8212\'20\'14lose the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) support at $3.35.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, today\u8217\'20\'19s drop in the crypto market is preceded by a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergence between its price and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/here-s-3-ways-the-relative-strength-index-rsi-can-be-used-as-a-sell-signal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relative strength index}}}\uc2  (\uc2 RSI\uc2 ), as shown in the chart below.\par \par \uc2 Notably, TOTAL rose between Nov. 5 and Dec. 31, forming a series of higher lows. But, in the same period, its daily RSI descended, forming lower lows.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2025-01/0194450d-dfc2-7ae7-a7d2-88495223b139"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Federal Reserve, Central Bank, Bitcoin Price, Bitcoin \b  \highlight22Regulation\b0 \highlight22 , Economy, Markets, Stocks, Inflation, Interest Rate, Binance, Stablecoin}}}\par \par \uc2 TOTAL/USD daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/vVaH1e44/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8203\'20\'0B\u8203\'20\'0BA divergence between rising prices and a falling \uc2 RSI\uc2  indicates weakness in the prevailing uptrend, prompting traders to sell more at local highs.\par \par \uc2 If the selling intensifies, the crypto market will likely drop toward the $3.18 trillion support embraced by the ascending trendline. Note that this line has acted as support for TOTAL since the US election on Nov. 5.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, a resurgence in buying pressure could push the crypto market cap back above the 50-day SMA and toward the local high of $3.54 trillion reached on Jan. 6.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvODAzMjgxMmQtMWQ1MC00NmFiLWI5NjUtYTBjYjZkZDQxYTYz.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020250108el1800030\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
