\par\par \b \uc2 Crypto Price Analysis 12-18 BITCOIN: BTC, ETHEREUM: ETH, SOLANA: SOL, DOGECOIN: DOGE, UNISWAP: UNI, ALGORAND: ALGO, OPTIMISM: OP\b0\par\par\uc2 Amara Khatri \par \uc2 2,889 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 December 2024\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2024, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Sets Another All-Time High}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Major Altcoins Emerge As Top Performers}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP \b  \highlight22Bullish\b0 \highlight22  Following RLUSD Launch}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin-Ethereum Combo Fund To Lead Wave Of Crypto ETFs In 2025}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Algorand (ALGO) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Optimism (OP) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) reached an all-time high for the second consecutive day, going past $108,000 and reaching a peak of $108,286. However, the cryptocurrency declined dramatically after reaching this level and is currently trading below $104,000, down almost 3% over the past 24 hours. Traders are now eying the $110,000 mark and are increasing bets for further gains in the options market.\par \par \uc2 Markets registered a decline overall as Ethereum (ETH) slipped below $4,000 after registering a drop of almost 5%. Dogecoin (DOGE) also registered a fall of nearly 4%, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/ADA-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano (\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 )}}}\uc2  is down by 4.50%. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/LINK-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chainlink (LINK)}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/TRX-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tron (TRX)}}}\uc2 , Avalanche (AVAX), Toncoin (TON), Polkadot (DOT), and Aptos (APT) also registered notable declines. As a result, the crypto market cap is down almost 3% and is currently at $3.63 trillion.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Sets Another All-Time High\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2024/12/crypto-price-analysis-12-17-bitcoin-btc-ethereum-eth-solana-sol-arbitrum-arb-chainlink-link-toncoin-ton-fantom-ftm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)}}}\uc2  surged to a new all-time high of $108,268 late on Tuesday before declining dramatically to its current levels. BTC rose almost 2.2% on Tuesday to reach its latest milestone but could not push higher as it retreated thanks to growing selling pressure. The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest cryptocurrency has seen gains of over 150% this year, with traders confident it will hit $110,000 before the end of the year. Their confidence is highlighted by the increasing bets for further gains in the options market. Shiliang Tang, the president of crypto principal trading firm Arbelos Markets, stated,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen buyers of $110k-$120k and $110k-$125k call spreads in Jan expiry, as well as rolling up of long strikes from $100k/$105k to 120k+ strikes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 BTC surged past the $100,000 milestone less than two weeks ago after President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced he was nominating \uc2 Paul Atkins\uc2 , known for his pro-crypto views, as the incoming \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) Chair. Spot Bitcoin ETFs also registered strong inflows as institutional interest in the asset continued to spike. James Butterfill, the Head of Research at \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 , stated,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat is driving prices is the US election dividend, and in 2025, the prospects for the US owning Bitcoin as a strategic reserve asset (likely not priced according to Polymarket, which sees it as having only a 27 percent chance of happening), geopolitical instability, looser monetary policy \u8212\'20\'14 these factors are likely to remain supportive in 2025.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Major Altcoins Emerge As Top Performers\par \par \uc2 The crypto market cap surged past $3.7 trillion on Tuesday before declining to its current levels. Bitcoin (BTC) hit a new all-time high, while Ethereum (ETH) also registered gains before declining. With the US Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) starting its last meeting of the year on Tuesday, markets remained \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , anticipating a third consecutive rate cut decision. Market watchers anticipate the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2  will likely lower its benchmark interest rate by 25 basis points at the end of its two-day meeting. If the Fed delivers an expected rate cut, it will likely rekindle investor demand for risk assets and bring a wave of capital to BTC and other altcoins.\par \par \uc2 XRP \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  Following RLUSD Launch\par \par \uc2 With Ripple announcing the launch of the RLUSD stablecoin, analysts are turning \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on XRP, with some predicting its value could surge to $22 by 2025. Popular crypto analyst CrediBULL Crypto has predicted XRP\u8217\'20\'19s market capitalization could reach a staggering $1.2 trillion during the ongoing bull cycle, which could continue well into the new year. CrediBULL Crypto shared his analysis on X, stating,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CZoom out a little so you don\u8217\'20\'19t forget the big picture. The structure on XRP here looks so freaking clean and \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it\u8217\'20\'19s actually insane. Forget what happens on these lower time frames\u8212\'20\'14it\u8217\'20\'19s noise (for a non-trader), the big picture is incredibly and unequivocally \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 XRP has registered an impressive rally since November, with its value increasing by 500%. However, its momentum has waned after hitting resistance around the $2.88 mark, leading to a decline and a brief struggle to stay above the $2 level.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin-Ethereum Combo Fund To Lead Wave Of Crypto ETFs In 2025\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg ETF analyst Eric Balchnas has said he expects an exchange-traded fund tracking BTC and ETH to be the first in a wave of new crypto ETFs in 2025. Balchunas shared an analysis by fellow ETF analyst James Seyffart, stating,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe expect a wave of cryptocurrency ETFs next year, albeit not all at once. First out is likely the BTC + eth combo ETFs, then prob \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  (bc its fork of BTC = commodity), then HBAR (bc not labeled security), and then XRP/Solana (which have been labeled securities in pending lawsuits).\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Balchunas and Seyffart expect the first Bitcoin and Ethereum combo fund to be closely followed by a fund tracking \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  (LTC) or Hedera (HBAR). However, Seyffart noted that the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) had rejected multiple Solana ETFs, adding that SOL and XRP ETFs would have to wait until \uc2 Paul Atkins\uc2  took charge of the SEC before being seriously considered. Balchunas believes regulators view LTC and HBAR more favorably, so they would get ETFs before assets like XRP and SOL.\par \par \uc2 LTC is likely to be greenlit because it is a fork of BTC and could be viewed as a commodity. Meanwhile, the SEC does not view HBAR as a security by the SEC, which could make it easier for it to receive approval.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/BTC-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)}}}\uc2  went past $108,000 late on Tuesday, setting yet another all-time high before declining rapidly during the current session, with the price currently at $103,760. But what is driving BTC\u8217\'20\'19s latest surge, and could growing institutional interest lead to a supply squeeze? BTC\u8217\'20\'19s post-election gains stand well over 50%, with its most recent rally beginning after President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  proposed establishing a US Bitcoin Strategic reserve, which sparked considerable excitement in the market.\par \par \uc2 Another major factor driving the rally is growing institutional interest and activity, particularly from \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2 . The company recently purchased its latest tranche of BTC worth $1.5 billion, bringing its total holdings to a staggering 439,000 BTC, valued around $48 billion at current prices. \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s inclusion in the Nasdaq 100 index is also expected to significantly boost demand for its stocks, which could positively impact BTC.\par \par \uc2 BTC\u8217\'20\'19s price action was mixed last week, as it registered a substantial drop on Monday, dropping almost 4% to an intraday low of $94,185 before settling at $97,434. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment persisted on Tuesday, with the price dropping to a low of $94,313 before settling at $96,912. BTC recovered on Wednesday to register an increase of just over 4% to climb above $100,000 and settled at $100,900. Despite positive price action on Wednesday, BTC fell back on Thursday, dropping by 0.97% and settling at $99,923. A recovery on Friday allowed BTC to reclaim the $100,000 level and settle at $101,394.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/NbejQ6OK/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 The weekend began with BTC registering a marginal decline on Saturday before rising almost 3% on Sunday to settle at $104,181. BTC surged to an intraday high of $107,464 to set an all-time high on Monday as \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment gathered pace. However, it could not stay at this level and ultimately settled at $105,750, registering an increase of 1.51%. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment persisted on Tuesday as BTC set a new all-time high, rising to $108,268 before declining and setting at $106,144. However, BTC declined during the current session, with the price down almost 2% at $104,246.\par \par \uc2 Despite the decline during the current session, analysts are confident BTC will surpass $110,000 before the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/ETH-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH)}}}\uc2  dropped considerably after briefly crossing $4,000 at the beginning of the week as it failed to consolidate above it yet again allowing sellers to drive the price lower. ETH has been \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the US elections but registered a substantial drop at the beginning of last week, falling over 7% to a low of $3,536 before settling at $3,715. The price continued to drop on Tuesday, falling 2.30% to $3,630. However, ETH brushed aside the growing \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment on Wednesday, registering an increase of 5.62% and settling at $3,834. Buyers retained control on Thursday as ETH rallied to an intraday high of $3,988. It lost momentum at this level and dropped to settle at $3,882, ultimately registering an increase of 1.26%. ETH went above $3,900 on Friday after rising 0.63% and settling at $3,907.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/wQ8Gi3XY/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Despite registering considerable gains since Wednesday, ETH fell back on Saturday, dropping almost 1% to go below $3,900 and settle at $3,869. However, buyers returned to the market on Sunday as ETH rose 2.25% and settled at $3,956. The current week began with ETH experiencing significant \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  as buyers and sellers attempted to establish control. As a result, ETH fell to an intraday low of $3,882 and rose to an intraday high of $4,106 before settling at $3,985. ETH fell into the red on Tuesday as sellers returned to the market, dropping by 2.34% and settling at $3,982. The current session sees ETH continue to decline, with the price down just over 1% and trading around $3,850.\par \par \uc2 If sellers can drive ETH below the 20-day SMA, it could drop to $3,500 before recovering. On the other hand, buyers will attempt to regain control and reclaim $4,000.\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  (SOL) continues to trade in a downward trajectory, with sellers having driven it below the 50-day SMA. SOL suffered a substantial drop at the beginning of the previous week as sellers decisively took control and lowered the price by 8.55% to $216. Sellers attempted to drive SOL below $200 on Tuesday as it fell to an intraday low of $203, briefly slipping below the 20-day SMA. However, it recovered partially to go above the 20-day SMA and settle at $213, ultimately registering a drop of 1.47%. Despite the selling pressure, SOL recovered on Wednesday, rising over 6% and settling at $227. Buyers attempted to push SOL above the 20-day SMA on Thursday as it reached an intraday high of $234. However, they lost momentum after reaching this level and SOL dropped to $227, registering a marginal decline.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/P4ifklYP/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment persisted on Friday as SOL dropped almost 1% and settled at $224, and intensified on Saturday as the price fell to a low of $215 before settling at $219. SOL recovered on Sunday, registering an increase of almost 2%, but fell on Monday, dropping 3.55% to go below the 50-day SMA and settle at $216. Tuesday saw \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  return as SOL dropped to an intraday low of $211 and reached an intraday high of $228. Buyers ultimately gained the upper hand and SOL settled at $223 after an increase of 3.23%. However, the current session sees SOL back in the red, with the price down almost 3% and trading at $216.\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/DOGE-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE)}}}\uc2  is struggling to recover after slipping below the 20-day SMA and has slipped below key support levels during the current session. DOGE experienced a significant drop on Monday as it fell over 11% to go below the 20-day SMA and settle at $0.414. Sellers continued to dominate on Tuesday as DOGE dropped almost 5% to $0.394. DOGE recovered on Wednesday, rising over 5% and settling at $0.414. However, despite the substantial increase, DOGE could not move past the 20-day SMA. As a result, it fell back on Thursday, dropping just over 2% and settling at $0.406. DOGE registered a marginal recovery on Friday, rising 0.89% and settling at $0.409.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/TvXxNqrs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 With the 20-day SMA acting as a dynamic resistance level, DOGE fell back in the red on Saturday, dropping just over 3% and settling at $0.397. It recovered on Sunday to register an increase of 2.19% and end the weekend positively. However, \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment returned on Monday as DOGE failed to go above the 20-day SMA, allowing sellers to take control. As a result, DOGE dropped just over 1% and settled at $0.401. Sellers retained control on Tuesday, driving DOGE below $0.40 to $0.393. The current session sees DOGE down almost 3% and trading around $0.383.\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI)\u8217\'20\'19s bull run came to an abrupt halt last Sunday after peaking at an intraday high of $19.47. UNI failed to stay at this level and plummeted on Monday, dropping almost 14% to $16.05. Sellers retained control on Tuesday a UNI dropped to an intraday low of $14.05 before recovering to settle at $15.24, ultimately registering a drop of just over 5%. UNI recovered on Wednesday, rising almost 13% and moving to $17.15. Buyers attempted to push UNI above the resistance at $19 as it surged to an intraday high of $18.98. However, UNI lost momentum in the face of selling pressure and dropped to $17.69, ultimately registering an increase of just over 3%.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/AlvzsrgA/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 With momentum waning, UNI fell into the red on Friday, dropping just over 1% and settling at $17.49. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment increased on Saturday as UNI dropped 4.28% to $16.75. However, it recovered on Sunday to register an increase of 1.69% and ended the weekend at $17.03. The current week began with sellers in control, as UNI dropped almost 5% to $16.23. The price registered a marginal increase on Tuesday, trading at $16.29 during the ongoing session.\par \par \uc2 Algorand (ALGO) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Algorand (ALGO) is trading between $0.40 and $0.45, attempting to build momentum and go back above the 20-day SMA. ALGO fell to an intraday low of $0.352 last Monday as it plummeted over 16%. However, it recovered on Tuesday, rising by 1.55% and settling at $0.423. Buyers retained control on Wednesday as ALGO registered an increase of just over 7% and settled at $0.453. However, sentiment changed on Thursday as ALGO dropped by 5.53% and settled at $0.428. The price recovered on Friday, rising by 2.27% and settling at $0.437.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/Qd4F74zI/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 However, ALGO was back in the red on Saturday, dropping almost 4% to slip below the 20-day SMA and settle at $0.420. The price rebounded on Sunday, recovering from a low of $0.406 to register an increase of 2.65% and settle at $0.431. The current week began with ALGO dropping over 4% and settling at $0.413. Buyers attempted a recovery on Tuesday as ALGO reached an intraday high of $0.442. However, it lost momentum after reaching this level and dropped to $0.412. The current session sees ALGO down almost 3% as sellers look to drive it below the $0.40 support level.\par \par \uc2 Optimism (OP) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Optimism (OP) is struggling to recover after suffering a considerable decline over the past few sessions. The price plummeted last Monday, dropping almost 16% to go below the 20-day SMA and settle at $2.24, but not before falling to an intraday low of $2.01. Sellers retained control on Tuesday as OP dropped to a low of $2.03 before settling at $2.20. OP recovered from this level on Wednesday, rising almost 6% and settling at $2.33. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified on Thursday as OP went above the 20-day SMA after an increase of 9.21% and settled at $2.55. Friday saw OP experience considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  as buyers and sellers struggled to establish control. Buyers ultimately gained the upper hand as OP registered a marginal increase and settled at $2.56.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/BRVJxVwQ/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 OP turned \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Saturday as buyers lost momentum. As a result, the price fell over 5% to slip below the 20-day SMA and settle at $2.43. However, it recovered on Sunday to go above the 20-day SMA again after registering an increase of just over 4% to settle at $2.53. OP fell on Monday, dropping by 1.58% and settling at $2.49. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified on Tuesday as OP dropped 6.45%, going below the 20-day SMA and settling at $2.33. The current session sees OP marginally up as buyers look to push back towards $2.50.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This article is provided for informational purposes only. It is not offered or intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, financial, or other advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020241219ekci00012\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 12/18: BTC, ETH, XRP, SOL, BNB, DOGE,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 AVAX\uc2 , LINK, SHIB\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,805 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 December 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and select altcoins are retracing their recent rally, indicating profit booking by the buyers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMTIvMDE5M2RhYjEtN2NhNC03Y2Y3LTg5NTgtOGJkOWM1NDczZDdl.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Price analysis 12/18: BTC, ETH, XRP, SOL, BNB, DOGE, \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 , AVAX, LINK, SHIB}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-108k-all-time-high-lasts-seconds-btc-price-dives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pulled back after making a new all-time high}}}\uc2  above $108,000 on Dec. 17, indicating that the bears have not given up and are selling on rallies. BitMEX co-founder \uc2 Arthur Hayes\uc2  wrote in his \u8220\'20\'1CTrump Truth\u8221\'20\'1D blog post that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/arthur-hayes-crypto-crash-donald-trump-inauguration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crypto markets are likely to dump}}}\uc2  following United States President-elect Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration in January 2025. Hayes said that selling will occur after market participants realize that any crypto policy changes will take about a year to enact.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, \uc2 Bitfinex\uc2  analysts expect the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-200k-mid-2025-mild-corrections-bitfinex"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dips in Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s uptrend to be short-lived}}}\uc2  in 2025 due to institutional demand. They estimate Bitcoin to reach $145,000 by mid-2025 and potentially stretch to \u8220\'20\'1C$200,000 under favorable conditions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193daab-a2dd-778e-8006-190c08950f9a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg, Cryptocurrencies, Gold, BitMEX, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Price Analysis, Market Analysis, Bitcoin ETF, ETF}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto market data daily view. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Sustained buying by institutional investors boosted collective net assets in US Bitcoin exchange-traded funds (ETFs) to more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-etfs-flip-gold-funds-aum-k33-research"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $129 billion on Dec. 16}}}\uc2 , a tad higher than US gold ETFs, according to a post on X by Vetle Lund, K33 Research\u8217\'20\'19s head of research.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg ETF analyst \uc2 Eric Balchunas\uc2  said in a post on X that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cunreal\u8221\'20\'1D that Bitcoin ETFs were competing so closely with gold funds just 11 months after launch.\par \par \uc2 Could Bitcoin enter a consolidation in the near term, or will the uptrend resume? How will the altcoins behave? Let\u8217\'20\'19s analyze the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin bulls pushed the price above the resistance line of the ascending channel pattern on Dec. 16 and Dec. 17 but could not sustain the higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193daac-4025-75ee-98ce-bba9a25af4fa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg, Cryptocurrencies, Gold, BitMEX, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Price Analysis, Market Analysis, Bitcoin ETF, ETF}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 While the rising moving averages indicate an advantage to buyers, the negative divergence on the relative strength index (\uc2 RSI\uc2 ) suggests that the uptrend is losing steam. That increases the possibility of a consolidation in the near term.\par \par \uc2 The 20-day exponential moving average ($99,974) is the critical support to watch out for. If the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA with strength, the likelihood of a break above the resistance line increases. That could push the BTC/USDT pair to $113,331 and later to $125,000.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be invalidated in the near term if the price turns down and breaks below the support line. That could pull the price to the 50-day simple moving average ($90,839).\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) again turned down from the overhead resistance of $4,094 on Dec. 16, indicating that the bears are aggressively defending the level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193daac-d909-73dd-9d8c-72057a8839df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg, Cryptocurrencies, Gold, BitMEX, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Price Analysis, Market Analysis, Bitcoin ETF, ETF}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 The ETH/USDT pair has pulled back to the 20-day EMA ($3,775), which is an important level to watch out for. If the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA with force, it will improve the prospects of a rally above $4,094. If that happens, the pair may soar toward $4,500.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, a break and close below the 20-day EMA will signal that the bulls are losing their grip. The pair may plunge to the downtrend line, which is expected to attract strong buying by the bulls.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 XRP\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) relief rally rose above the near-term resistance of $2.65 on Dec. 17, but the bulls could not sustain the higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193daad-6fb7-78e8-97da-009fc6467cad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg, Cryptocurrencies, Gold, BitMEX, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Price Analysis, Market Analysis, Bitcoin ETF, ETF}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 If buyers do not give up much ground from the current level, the XRP/USDT pair could again rise above $2.65 and challenge the crucial overhead resistance of $2.91. A break and close above $2.91 could clear the path for a rally to $3.50.\par \par \uc2 If bears want to make a comeback, they will have to quickly tug the price below the 20-day EMA ($2.25). If they do that, the pair could plunge to the 61.8% Fibonacci retracement level of $1.90.\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  price analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) dipped below the 50-day SMA ($218) on Dec. 16, but the bulls defended the $210 support on Dec. 17.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193daae-0978-7368-adda-ff86f7836a4a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg, Cryptocurrencies, Gold, BitMEX, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Price Analysis, Market Analysis, Bitcoin ETF, ETF}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls failed to maintain the price above the 20-day EMA ($225), which has again pulled the SOL/USDT pair to $210. The repeated retest of a support level tends to weaken it. If the $210 support cracks, the pair could plunge to the support line of the descending channel pattern.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will be invalidated in the near term if the price turns up from $210 and rises above the channel\u8217\'20\'19s resistance line. The pair may then attempt a rally to $248.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) remains stuck inside a tight range between $722 and the 20-day EMA ($700), indicating a tough battle between the bulls and the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193daae-ae2a-7638-b990-ef8fa35dc0b9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg, Cryptocurrencies, Gold, BitMEX, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Price Analysis, Market Analysis, Bitcoin ETF, ETF}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down and breaks below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest advantage to the bears. The BNB/USDT pair could then tumble to the 50-day SMA ($649), which is likely to attract buyers.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the bulls pierce and maintain the price above the $722 resistance, it will signal a positive sentiment. The pair may climb to $761 and subsequently to $794.\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bears did not allow Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) to remain above the 20-day EMA ($0.40) on Dec. 16, which may have tempted short-term buyers to book profits.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193daaf-4daf-70ba-8f27-4dd1dd24152d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg, Cryptocurrencies, Gold, BitMEX, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Price Analysis, Market Analysis, Bitcoin ETF, ETF}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 That has pulled the DOGE/USDT pair toward the 50-day SMA ($0.35), which is a critical near-term support. Buyers are expected to vigorously defend the 50-day SMA, but the relief rally is likely to face strong selling at the 20-day EMA.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, it will signal that bears are selling on rallies. That increases the possibility of a break below the 50-day SMA. The pair may then drop to $0.30. If bulls want to prevent the downside, they will have to push and maintain the price above $0.43.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has slipped below the 20-day EMA ($1.05), indicating that the bulls are rushing to the exit.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193daaf-de51-79ce-badd-de1f83098c9d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg, Cryptocurrencies, Gold, BitMEX, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Price Analysis, Market Analysis, Bitcoin ETF, ETF}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is flattening out, and the \uc2 RSI\uc2  is near the midpoint, suggesting a possible range-bound action in the near term. Sellers will try to pull the price to $0.90, which is expected to act as a strong support.\par \par \uc2 The bulls will be back in the driver\u8217\'20\'19s seat after they push and maintain the price above $1.20. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could rise to $1.24 and eventually to $1.33, where the bears are likely to mount a strong defense.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-is-cardano-price-down-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why is Cardano price down today?}}}\par \par \uc2 Avalanche price analysis\par \par \uc2 Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) has broken below the 20-day EMA ($47.71), indicating a lack of demand from the bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193dab0-939d-7e31-a2fe-8c917ee9ca8b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg, Cryptocurrencies, Gold, BitMEX, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Price Analysis, Market Analysis, Bitcoin ETF, ETF}}}\par \par \uc2 AVAX\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below the 20-day EMA, the \uc2 AVAX\uc2 /USDT pair could drop to the 50-day SMA ($39.52). This is a critical level for the buyers to defend because a break below it will suggest that the breakout above $51 may have been a bull trap.\par \par \uc2 Instead, if the price turns up and rises above the 20-day EMA, it will signal buying at lower levels. The bulls will try to strengthen their position by pushing the price above $51 and then $56. If they manage to do that, the pair may travel toward $65.\par \par \uc2 Chainlink price analysis\par \par \uc2 Chainlink ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/chainlink-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LINK}}}\uc2  ) is correcting in an uptrend, suggesting that the short-term buyers are booking profits.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193dab1-2baa-7036-ad8a-84ee6850f39c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg, Cryptocurrencies, Gold, BitMEX, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Price Analysis, Market Analysis, Bitcoin ETF, ETF}}}\par \par \uc2 LINK/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 The negative divergence on the \uc2 RSI\uc2  suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum is weakening. If the price sustains below $27.41, the LINK/USDT pair could slump to the 20-day EMA ($24.85). This is a crucial level for the bulls to defend because a break below it may sink the pair to the breakout level of $23.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns up and maintains above $27.41, it will suggest solid buying on dips. The pair could then retest the overhead resistance at $31.\par \par \uc2 Shiba Inu price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bulls failed to push Shiba Inu ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/shiba-inu-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SHIB}}}\uc2  ) back above the 20-day EMA ($0.000027) on Dec. 16, attracting selling by the bears.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193dab1-ef52-72ff-8def-13a3a0086b45"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg, Cryptocurrencies, Gold, BitMEX, Markets, Cryptocurrency Exchange, Arthur Hayes, Donald Trump, Price Analysis, Market Analysis, Bitcoin ETF, ETF}}}\par \par \uc2 SHIB/USDT daily chart. Source: Cointelegraph/TradingView\par \par \uc2 That has pulled the price to the 50-day SMA ($0.000025), which is an important support to keep an eye on. The 20-day EMA has started to turn down, and the \uc2 RSI\uc2  has slipped into negative territory, indicating that the bulls are losing their grip. If the 50-day SMA cracks, the SHIB/USDT pair could descend to $0.000022 and later to $0.000020.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the price rebounds off the 50-day SMA with force, it will signal demand at lower levels. The bulls will then try to push the price above the 20-day EMA, opening the doors for a recovery to $0.000030.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMTIvMDE5M2RhYjEtN2NhNC03Y2Y3LTg5NTgtOGJkOWM1NDczZDdl.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020241218ekci000bb\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Why is the crypto market down today?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Nancy Lubale \par \uc2 977 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 December 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Cascading derivatives liquidations and risk-off mode ahead of the Fed rate decision appear to be factors in the current crypto market sell-off.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvODAzMjgxMmQtMWQ1MC00NmFiLWI5NjUtYTBjYjZkZDQxYTYz.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why is the crypto market down today?}}}\par \par \uc2 The cryptocurrency market took a hit today, with the total market capitalization dropping by around 3% to about $3.65 trillion on Dec. 18.\par \par \uc2 This sudden plunge has left many investors scratching their heads, trying to understand the core catalysts behind this downturn and whether more losses are on the horizon.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193d903-243e-7bbe-95e5-29b45d7774ca"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Federal Reserve, Central Bank, Bitcoin Price, Bitcoin \b  \highlight22Regulation\b0 \highlight22 , Economy, Markets, Stocks, Inflation, Interest Rate, Binance, Stablecoin}}}\par \par \uc2 24-hour performance of large-cap cryptocurrencies. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s look closer at the factors driving the crypto market down today.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin leads the market slump\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s crypto market decline is part of a correction that started during the late New York trading hours on Dec. 15 when Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-108k-all-time-high-lasts-seconds-btc-price-dives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tumbled from an all-time high of $108,364}}}\uc2  reached on Dec. 17 on \uc2 Bitstamp\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BTC price dropped as much as 5% to an intra-day low of $103,173 on Dec. 18. The decline in BTC triggered panic selling among crypto investors, with cryptocurrencies dropping across the board.\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) extended its two-day losses, dipping as low as $3,800 on Dec. 18, marking 4% losses over the last 24 hours.\par \par \uc2 Other top-cap cryptocurrencies posting significant losses on Dec. 16 are Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  )and Tron ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tron-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TRX}}}\uc2  ), which are down 3.4%, 3.4% and 6%, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Massive liquidations across the derivatives market accompanied this downturn in the crypto market.\par \par \uc2 Data from CoinGlass shows that a total of $419 million have been liquidated over the last 24 hours, with $333 million making up long positions. Long BTC leveraged positions totaling $53 million have also been liquidated on the day.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193d904-15ee-7d41-bc5a-95ed0c1d58d4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Federal Reserve, Central Bank, Bitcoin Price, Bitcoin \b  \highlight22Regulation\b0 \highlight22 , Economy, Markets, Stocks, Inflation, Interest Rate, Binance, Stablecoin}}}\par \par \uc2 Total crypto liquidations. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.coinglass.com/LiquidationData"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CoinGlass}}}\par \par \uc2 A similar move was seen on Dec. 9 in the derivatives market when more than $1.5 billion long positions were liquidated. These liquidations accompany an 11% drop in TOTAL\u8212\'20\'14the combined market capitalization of all cryptocurrencies\u8212\'20\'14with more than $400 billion being wiped off the crypto market.\par \par \uc2 A predominance of long liquidations suggests that the crypto market was overleveraged on the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  side, primarily due to profit-taking and risk-off mode ahead of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-price-base-case-140k-5-things-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 today\u8217\'20\'19s Fed decision}}}\uc2  on rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 Risk-off sentiment pushed the crypto market down\par \par \uc2 The ongoing correction in the crypto market mirrors the weakness witnessed in US equities. The S&P 500 dropped by 0.4% to close the day at 6,050.61 on Dec. 17, while the Nasdaq composite index declined by 64 points.\par \par \uc2 The Dow Jones index clocked its ninth consecutive daily loss, its longest losing streak since 1978, losing 0.61% to close the trading day on Dec. 17 at 43,339.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193d905-2cd1-7ec1-9653-593aaa9aea90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Federal Reserve, Central Bank, Bitcoin Price, Bitcoin \b  \highlight22Regulation\b0 \highlight22 , Economy, Markets, Stocks, Inflation, Interest Rate, Binance, Stablecoin}}}\par \par \uc2 24-hour performance of US equities Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finviz.com/map.ashx?t=sec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Financial Visualizations}}}\par \par \uc2 This performance highlights the impact of interest rate cuts on the valuation of the largest companies listed on stock exchanges in the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTomorrow marks the final Fed meeting of 2024,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KobeissiLetter/status/1869061296588767567"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  capital markets commentator The Kobeissi Letter in a Dec. 17 post on X.\par \par \uc2 As such, market participants have now turned their focus on the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interest rate cut decision later today.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cmegroup.com/markets/interest-rates/cme-fedwatch-tool.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from \uc2 CME Group\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s FedWatch Tool, the odds of the Fed keeping interest rates unchanged are now standing at 4.6% at the time of writing, against 95.4% for a 0.25% rate cut.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193d905-a66c-75d1-aa7c-b67ff24c4c36"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Federal Reserve, Central Bank, Bitcoin Price, Bitcoin \b  \highlight22Regulation\b0 \highlight22 , Economy, Markets, Stocks, Inflation, Interest Rate, Binance, Stablecoin}}}\par \par \uc2 Fed target rate probabilities for Dec. 18 FOMC meeting. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cmegroup.com/markets/interest-rates/cme-fedwatch-tool.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CME Group}}}\par \par \uc2 A 25 basis points cut will mark the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s third rate cut of 2024, bringing the total reduction to 100 basis points.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMeanwhile, CPI, PPI, and PCE inflation are all back on the rise as the labor market weakens,\u8221\'20\'1D The Kobeissi Letter noted, adding:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll eyes will be on the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s outlook for 2025 as the fight against inflation is not over yet. The Fed has a tough job ahead.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/stablecoins-will-see-explosive-growth-in-2025-as-world-embraces-asset-class"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stablecoins will see explosive growth in 2025 as world embraces asset class}}}\par \par \uc2 TOTAL\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergence\par \par \uc2 Today\u8217\'20\'19s drop in the crypto market is preceded by a growing \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergence between its price and the relative strength index (\uc2 RSI\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 Notably, TOTAL rose between Nov. 11 and Dec. 17, forming a series of higher highs. But, in the same period, its daily RSI descended, forming lower highs.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193d906-525a-7971-8374-62cf0818c66f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Federal Reserve, Central Bank, Bitcoin Price, Bitcoin \b  \highlight22Regulation\b0 \highlight22 , Economy, Markets, Stocks, Inflation, Interest Rate, Binance, Stablecoin}}}\par \par \uc2 TOTAL/USD daily chart. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/AVe62ZJS/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 A divergence between rising prices and a falling \uc2 RSI\uc2  indicates weakness in the prevailing uptrend, which could hint at a reversal ahead.\par \par \uc2 The consistent rise in TOTAL also led to overbought conditions for most of the period between Nov. 11 and Dec. 8, when the \uc2 RSI\uc2  moved above 70, occasioning a correction as buyer exhaustion and profit-booking set in.\par \par \uc2 If the selling intensifies, the crypto market will likely drop toward the $3.50 trillion support embraced by the ascending trendline. Note that this line has acted as a dynamic support for TOTAL since Nov. 11.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, a resurgence in buying pressure could push the crypto market cap toward its all-time high of $3.73 trillion, reached on Dec. 16.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvODAzMjgxMmQtMWQ1MC00NmFiLWI5NjUtYTBjYjZkZDQxYTYz.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020241218ekci0005r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
