\par\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin: Navigating the  \highlight22\uc2 Bullish \highlight\uc2  Battle Above $100K\b0\par\par\uc2 Michal D. Ciesla \par \uc2 1,506 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 December 2024\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2024, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin: Navigating the \b  \highlight22Bullish\b0 \highlight22  Battle Above $100K}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ls-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Rectangle Pattern and $74K Support}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ls-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The $107K Bull Flag: Still in Play?}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ls-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Rising Wedge and Current Challenges}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ls-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Momentum Check: RSI Signals Mixed but Worrisome}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ls-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Key Ideas to Trade This}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Summary: A Complicated Saturday Night}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin: Navigating the \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  Battle Above $100K\par \par \uc2 This weekend has failed to deliver the relief retail traders hoped for, bringing more retracements and the emergence of \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  patterns. The highly anticipated "Santa rally" seems increasingly out of reach as macroeconomic uncertainty weighs heavily on the market.\par \par \uc2 Several major cryptocurrencies are underperforming today, with notable losers including SUI ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/sui/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $SUI}}}\uc2  ), down 6.5% after peaking at its all-time high of $4.89 last Friday, along with PEPE {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/pepe/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ($PEPE}}}\uc2  ), BONK {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/bonk1/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ($BONK}}}\uc2  ), and Polkadot {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/polkadot-new/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ($DOT}}}\uc2  ), all dropping roughly 6%. Adding to the downturn, Cardano {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/cardano/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ($\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Fantom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/fantom/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ($FTM}}}\uc2  ), and Hedera {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2024/12/hbar-at-a-turning-point-pepe-moonshot-ahead-and-tits-ready-to-explode-crypto-weekend-showdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ($HBAR}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 click for full insight) have each fallen by over 5%, reflecting a broad retreat across the altcoin market.\par \par \uc2 The global crypto market cap currently sits at $3.6 trillion, marking a 1.2% decline in the past 24 hours, while trading volume has dropped sharply by 23.93% (typical for Saturday). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/bitcoin/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin}}}\uc2  's dominance has increased slightly to 55.74%, as investors shift toward safer bets amid the growing uncertainty. Meanwhile, the Altcoin Season Index on CoinMarketCapsuggests Bitcoin remains firmly in control of the market, leaving altcoins struggling to gain traction.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s easy to feel pessimistic in moments like these, but seasoned investors know the drill. After all, if you\u8217\'20\'19ve been through a few of these wild four-year cycles, the strategy remains the same: zoom out, ignore the noise, and prepare for strategic buying opportunities.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s break down the market leader, the king of cryptocurrencies: Bitcoin ($BTC):\par \par \uc2 The Rectangle Pattern and $74K Support\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s first address the elephant in the room: the rectangle pattern that formed back in February this year, shortly after the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 ETF approval\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January 2024. This pattern broke to the upside on the election results, hitting its full target of $99,000 perfectly before becoming a strong resistance level (now flipped into main short-term support). Now, the rectangle\u8217\'20\'19s upper edge at $74,000 is playing a critical support role, often considered the \u8220\'20\'1Cline in the sand\u8221\'20\'1D for many BTC investors.\par \par \uc2 Adding further support to this rectangle is the 200-day moving average (green line), which currently sits at $69,000 and is gaining upside momentum. Historically, the 200-day MA serves as a strong dynamic support in bull markets. However, Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s significant decoupling above this level also raises concerns of a potential return-to-mean scenario, which could see the price retrace to align with this long-term trend. Have a good look at 1d:\par \par \uc2 If $74,000 were to break with confirmation, it could trigger a wave of exits, with the next logical stop being a test of the rectangle\u8217\'20\'19s bottom around $49,000\u8211\'20\'13$50,000. While such a correction doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have to happen (or at least not until the next bear market), it\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that a breakdown to $74K would represent a 27-28% retracement from the ATH. Brutal as it sounds, this would be a relatively normal correction within a BTC bull market.\par \par \uc2 The $107K Bull Flag: Still in Play?\par \par \uc2 One of the most significant \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  macro formations for Bitcoin this year began with the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s groundbreaking \b \highlight22\uc2 ETF approval\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The January\u8211\'20\'13May 2024 bull flag (green on the 1D chart) remains active, with a clear target at $107,000. This target is no joke, especially since the flag\u8217\'20\'19s lower trendline extension has acted as a reversal point three times, reinforcing its significance.\par \par \uc2 Interestingly, on the 4-hour chart, another \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pennant pattern (purple) mirrors this flag\u8217\'20\'19s target at $107,500. Two independent patterns aligning at the same price level give further weight to this target, making it a key projected take-profit zone.\par \par \uc2 This alignment of patterns illustrates Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s broader \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  potential, provided short-term challenges don\u8217\'20\'19t derail momentum.\par \par \uc2 The Rising Wedge and Current Challenges\par \par \uc2 While the long-term outlook points higher, BTC is currently trapped in a rising wedge on the 4-hour chart, a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pattern by classical charting standards. Notably, the wedge\u8217\'20\'19s bottom was formed by two significant December flash crashes, which now act as critical levels to watch.\par \par \uc2 $101,000 is holding\u8212\'20\'14for now. While Bitcoin briefly broke above six figures, the breakout lacked volume confirmation and momentum, leaving the price vulnerable to a pullback. By the time you read this, the $100K+ price might already be history.\par \par \uc2 If the rising wedge breaks down, the target aligns almost perfectly with the 0.382 Fibonacci level just below $87,000.\par \par \uc2 A close below $90,000 would also invalidate the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  pennant pattern, significantly weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  case.\par \par \uc2 Momentum Check: RSI Signals Mixed but Worrisome\par \par \uc2 The daily \uc2 RSI\uc2  remains relatively \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19, currently holding just above 64 after cooling down from an overbought period in November. This steady position is supported by a strong \uc2 RSI\uc2  trendline that has been rising since August 2024 (visible in the chart as the red trendline). As long as \uc2 RSI\uc2  respects this trendline and continues its gradual upward movement, Bitcoin retains the momentum for further gains.\par \par \uc2 However, concerns arise when we analyze the 4-hour RSI, which reveals signs of exhaustion. The \uc2 RSI\uc2  only reached 76 during BTC\u8217\'20\'19s December 5 ATH of $103,700, forming a lower high compared to earlier overbought readings. This is an example of \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  divergence, where price makes a higher high while \uc2 RSI\uc2  makes a lower high. In simpler terms, this means that while the price climbed, the underlying momentum weakened\u8212\'20\'14a classic red flag that often precedes corrections or consolidations.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the mixed sentiment, volume during BTC\u8217\'20\'19s breakout above $100,000 was lackluster, a classic red flag for sustainability in \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  price action.\par \par \uc2 As of now, Bitcoin remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  as long as it holds above the 50-day SMA (yellow line) on the daily chart, currently sitting near $99,000, which also aligns with a key horizontal support level. For bulls to regain full control, the wedge must be invalidated by a strong daily close above $103,000, preferably with a notable volume spike.\par \par \uc2 Key Ideas to Trade This\par \par \uc2 Breakout Above $103K:\par \par \uc2 A strong daily close above $103,000 with a clear volume spike would invalidate the wedge and signal momentum to target $107K. Watch for follow-through on the 4-hour timeframe to confirm the breakout.\par \par \uc2 Trading the Wedge:\par \par \uc2 Use the lower trendline of the wedge for potential long entries on price reversals. Confirmation can come from \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  candle patterns (e.g., hammers) or \uc2 RSI\uc2  rebounding from oversold zones.\par \par \uc2 Do Nothing:\par \par \uc2 The safest strategy is most likely to just wait. With the FOMC meeting looming on Wednesday, markets are likely to remain hesitant. Instead, consider scouting for entry points to capitalize on a likely retracement (Sunday to Monday night would be my guess).\par \par \uc2 Summary: A Complicated Saturday Night\par \par \uc2 As of Saturday night, Bitcoin remains in a delicate situation. Trading above the short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  50 SMA (yellow line) on the daily chart and holding the horizontal support at $99,000 keeps BTC in a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  posture. However, for the king to truly stay strong on this timeframe, the rising wedge must be invalidated with a strong close above $103,000, preferably backed by a significant volume spike.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the complexity, the Fear & Greed Index has returned to Extreme Greed (80) territory, following a brief dip during recent liquidations.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://coinmarketcap.com/}}}\par \par \uc2 The problem? Those liquidations failed to reset sentiment properly, leaving the market overly optimistic without clearing enough leverage. This makes the current setup even more perilous, as excessive greed often precedes sharp corrections.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Altcoin Season Index currently sits at 60, signaling a phase of indecision. While the index remains above neutral territory, the sharp drop from last week's 83 confirms what we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing across the market: altcoin season is suspended\u8212\'20\'14not entirely called off, but certainly losing steam. Altcoins will likely continue struggling until Bitcoin (and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/currencies/ethereum/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $ETH}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2024/12/is-the-altcoin-season-still-coming-back-in-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 link}}}\uc2  to analysis) either consolidates with strength or resolves its current patterns.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s be real\u8212\'20\'14this article could feel outdated by Monday if BTC does print a decisive candle soon to target the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  patterns described. December, despite Moonvember\u8217\'20\'19s fantastic run, has been tougher than expected. The crypto market is undoubtedly more complex now than last month\u8212\'20\'14or even last weekend.\par \par \uc2 The easy part of this bull market is over. Santa or no Santa, things are about to get wild. And when Trump takes office alongside the new, allegedly crypto-friendly leadership, we\u8217\'20\'19ll be in for a market environment no one\u8217\'20\'19s truly prepared for.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This article is provided for informational purposes only. It is not offered or intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, financial, or other advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020241216ekcf0000d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
