\par\par \b \uc2 Crypto Price Analysis 12-9 BITCOIN: BTC, ETHEREUM: ETH, SOLANA: SOL, LITECOIN: LTC, CHAINLINK: LINK, UNISWAP: UNI, CELESTIA: TIA\b0\par\par\uc2 Amara Khatri \par \uc2 2,609 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2024\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2024, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 Table of Contents\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BlackRock Spot Bitcoin ETF Crosses 500,000 BTC}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Corporations Increase BTC Holdings}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto Industry Frustrated Over Anti-Crypto Commissioner Vote}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iran Embraces Crypto To Counter Sanctions}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Litecoin (LTC) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chainlink (LINK) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cryptodaily.co.uk/#ms-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Celestia (TIA) Price Analysis}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) dipped below the $100,000 level earlier today as its price continues to consolidate while facing resistance around the $101,000 mark. The price had risen to $101,267 early during trading but fell considerably to a low of $99,113 before marginally recovering to settle at its current level. The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest cryptocurrency has gained almost 50% since Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election victory but is down by 1.25% over the past 24 hours as it consolidates around the $100,000 mark.\par \par \uc2 The crypto market has started the week in the red, with almost all major cryptocurrencies firmly in the red. These include Ethereum (ETH), which is down almost 2%, and Ripple (XRP), down nearly 5%, and Solana (SOL), down almost 4%. Significant losses were also recorded by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/DOGE-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dogecoin (DOGE)}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/ADA-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano (\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 )}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/TRX-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tron (TRX)}}}\uc2 , Toncoin (TON), Polkadot (DOT), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/XLM-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stellar (XLM)}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/BCH-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin Cash (BCH)}}}\uc2 . However, Chainlink (LINK) bucked the trend, registering a substantial increase of almost 10%. Thanks to these losses, the crypto market cap has declined by nearly 2% and currently sits at $3.62 trillion.\par \par \uc2 BlackRock Spot Bitcoin ETF Crosses 500,000 BTC\par \par \uc2 BlackRock\u8217\'20\'19s iShares {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/2024/12/crypto-price-analysis-12-6-bitcoin-btc-ethereum-eth-solana-sol-litecoin-ltc-cardano-ada-arbitrum-arb-algorand-algo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin}}}\uc2  Trust ETF\u8217\'20\'19s latest purchase of 7,750 BTC worth $253 million took IBIT\u8217\'20\'19s total BTC balance past 500,000 BTC, making it one of the largest private company holders of the asset. The latest purchase also demonstrates growing confidence in BTC as an asset for investing and wealth management. BlackRock\u8217\'20\'19s spot Bitcoin ETF crossed $50 billion in assets under management within 228 days of its launch, highlighting growing interest among traders who want to gain exposure to the asset through regulated commercial products. Spot Bitcoin ETFs also make it easy for entrepreneurs to access cryptocurrency markets without managing wallets or private keys.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLATEST: BlackRock\u8217\'20\'19s $IBIT bought $253.2M worth of Bitcoin on Dec. 6. That makes a total of $2.6 billion of inflows this week for $IBIT.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 BTC has seen a steady stream of interest from institutions and major corporations, with analysts observing that demand from new shareholders is helping BTC test new highs. BTC\u8217\'20\'19s growing popularity is also changing its perception from that of a speculative asset to a reliable investment option.\par \par \uc2 Corporations Increase BTC Holdings\par \par \uc2 Several corporations, including MicroStrategy and MARA Holdings, have significantly increased their BTC reserves. MicroStrategy acquired 15,400 BTC for $1.5 billion, increasing its total portfolio to a staggering 402,100 BTC. MARA Holdings purchased 6,484 BTC between October and November for $618 million, bringing its total BTC reserves to 34,794 BTC, making it the second-largest corporate holder of the asset.\par \par \uc2 Crypto Industry Frustrated Over Anti-Crypto Commissioner Vote\par \par \uc2 The United States Senate Banking Committee is set to vote on whether to renominate Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) commissioner Caroline Crenshaw, a vocal critic of cryptocurrencies. Industry executives have voiced considerable frustration on the possibility of her re-election. Crenshaw also voted against approving spot Bitcoin ETFs in January. Coinbase president and COO Emilie Choi criticized the potential re-election, stating the \u8220\'20\'1CSEC has to change\u8221\'20\'1D in a post on X.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCaroline Crenshaw is anti-crypto. She even embarrassingly opposed Bitcoin ETFs. The SEC has to change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Crypto investment firm Paradigm\u8217\'20\'19s government affairs VP Alexander Grieve called the re-election one last gift for crypto on the way out the door, stating,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs one last \u8220\'20\'1Cgift\u8221\'20\'1D for crypto on the way out the door, Senate Banking Chair Sherrod Brown is trying to ram through the renomination of anti-crypto SEC commissioner Caroline Crenshaw. Committee vote set for next Wednesday.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg ETF analyst James Seyffart stated,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe wasn't just "an ally to Gensler" IMO -- she was more vehemently anti-crypto than Gensler. Just read through her dissent letter on the Bitcoin ETF approvals back in January (The other dem commissioner, Liz\u225\'00\'E1rraga, didn't even join her on that letter).\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Iran Embraces Crypto To Counter Sanctions\par \par \uc2 Iran has shifted its stance on crypto, focusing on \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than restrictions, according to Minister Abdolnaser Hemmati. Hemmati highlighted the Iranian government\u8217\'20\'19s plans to mitigate the economic risks of digital currencies while leveraging their potential benefits. He also stressed the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s authority in managing digital assets and highlighted their potential to foster economic growth, provide employment opportunities, and counter sanctions.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/BTC-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin (BTC)}}}\uc2  has continued to trade in range as it consolidates before its next big move. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment has waned as the price faces significant resistance around the $101,000 mark. The price had dipped to a low of $90,708 on November 26 but rebounded to clear crucial resistance levels at $96,000 and $98,000, eventually creating history by going above $100,000 and setting a new all-time high of $103,900.\par \par \uc2 BTC started the previous week on a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  note, registering a drop of 1.25% on Monday and settling at $95,812. Selling pressure intensified on Tuesday as BTC briefly dipped below the 20-day SMA, dropping to a low of $93,763. However, it recovered from this level to climb above $95,000 and settle at $95,751. The price recovered on Wednesday, registering a substantial jump of almost 3% and settling at $98,851. Thursday saw unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a historic moment as BTC surged past $100,000. The day began with sellers in control as BTC dropped to an intraday low of $92,285. However, it recovered from this level to surge past $100,000 and set a new all-time high of $103,900 before settling at $97,093.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/MEaVMNkV/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC breached the $100,000 mark again on Friday, rising to an intraday high of $101,911. However, it could not stay above $100,000 and fell to $99,695, registering an increase of 2.68%. BTC remained positive over the weekend, registering a marginal increase on Saturday before rising by 1.32% on Sunday to end the weekend above $100,000 at $101,043. However, BTC has slipped below $100,000 during the current session, with the price down just over 2% and trading at $98,898.\par \par \uc2 So where does BTC go from here? BTC is facing resistance around the $101,000 mark. If it fails to go above this level, we could see a decline, with immediate support around $99,000. The next support levels lie at $97,500 and $95,000. On the other hand, if buyers retake control, BTC could push towards the $105,000 mark.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum (ETH) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/ETH-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum (ETH)}}}\uc2  struggled to move above the resistance at $4,000, with the price dropping considerably during the ongoing session. ETH started the previous week in the red, falling almost 2% to $3,645. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified on Tuesday as ETH dropped to a low of $3,504. However, it recovered from this level to settle at $3,617, eventually registering a marginal increase. However, ETH made a strong recovery on Wednesday, rising over 6% and going past the resistance at $3,700 to settle at $3,844. The price experienced significant \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday as buyers and sellers attempted to take control. As a result, ETH rose to an intraday high of $3,957 and fell to an intraday low of $3,644 before settling at $3,787, ultimately registering a drop of 1.48%.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/lcqFb7ZS/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH recovered on Friday as it surged past $4,000 to an intraday high of $4,093. However, it could not stay at this level and declined to $4,003, registering an increase of 5.71%. Saturday saw ETH register a marginal drop as sellers attempted to lower the price, and buyers attempted to push the price higher before ETH settled at $3,999. Sellers tried to take control on Sunday and drive ETH towards $3,800 as the price dropped to a low of $3,924. However, it recovered from this level to register a marginal increase and settle at $4,007. The current session sees sellers firmly in control, with ETH down over 3% and trading at $3,875.\par \par \uc2 ETH faces resistance at $4,000, a level it is struggling to overcome. If buyers can go above this level, a move to $4,250 could materialize. On the other hand, if sellers retain control, we could see the \b \highlight22\uc2 price drop\b0 \highlight\uc2  as low as $3,500.\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana (SOL started the current week with a substantial decline as selling pressure registered a considerable increase. The altcoin had started the previous week with a significant drop, falling almost 5% to slip below the 20-day SMA and settle at $225, but not before dropping to an intraday low of $219. Sellers pushed SOL to an intraday low of $215 on Tuesday as \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment persisted. However, SOL recovered from this level to register an increase of almost 4% and settle at $234. Buyers attempted a move past the 20-day SMA on Wednesday as SOL reached an intraday high of $241. However, buyers lost momentum after reaching this level, and SOL fell by almost 2% to $229.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/80juLcf0/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased substantially on Thursday as SOL fell to an intraday low of $221 and reached an intraday high of $244 before dipping below the 20-day SMA and settling at $236, registering an increase of almost 3%. Buyers lost momentum on Friday, thanks to the 20-day SMA acting as a dynamic resistance level. As a result, SOL registered only a marginal increase and settled at $237. The weekend was mixed for SOL as it registered a marginal increase of 0.51% on Saturday before dropping by 0.48% on Sunday to settle at $237. However, selling pressure has intensified considerably during the current session, with SOL down almost 4% and trading at $227. If sellers retain control, SOL could drop to $220. A breach of this support level could drive the price to $200.\par \par \uc2 Litecoin (LTC) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/LTC-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Litecoin (LTC)}}}\uc2  has been highly \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  during recent sessions, but momentum waned towards the end of last week, with \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  and selling pressure increasing substantially. LTC surged over 16% last Sunday, going above crucial resistance levels and settling at $119. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment persisted on Monday as LTC rose almost 11% to go above $130 and settle at $132. Despite a strong start to the week, LTC fell to a low of $121 on Tuesday as \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment returned. The price ultimately settled at $130, registering a drop of 1.43%. LTC registered another dramatic fall on Wednesday as it dropped to $121 before recovering to register an increase of 2.23% and settle at $133.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/I8ZPyHna/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  registered a substantial increase on Thursday as LTC rose to an intraday high of $147 and fell to an intraday low of $125 before settling at $135, registering an increase of 1.43%. With sellers active at this level, LTC could only register a marginal rise on Friday and settle at $136. However, it fell on Saturday, dropping almost 1.67% and settling at $133. Buyers propped up the price on Sunday as LTC registered an increase of 0.90% and settled at $134. However, LTC has registered a substantial drop during the ongoing session, with the price down over 8% and trading at $123.\par \par \uc2 Chainlink (LINK) Price Analysis\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/finance/quote/LINK-USD?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chainlink (LINK)}}}\uc2  started the previous week with an unprecedented surge, registering an increase of almost 34% to go above $20 and settle at $25. However, buyers lost momentum on Tuesday, allowing sellers to take control. As a result, LINK dropped over 4% and settled at $24.12. Buyers attempted a recovery on Wednesday as LINK surged above the resistance at $25 and settled at $26.52. However, it could not stay at this level and fell to $24.10, registering a marginal decline. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment persisted on Thursday as LINK dropped almost 4% to $23.15. Despite selling pressure, LINK recovered on Friday, rallying nearly 12% to go above $25 and settle at $25.88.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/sNI3aDog/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 Sellers returned to the market on Saturday as LINK dropped over 4% to go below $25 and settle at $24.81. However, positive sentiment returned on Sunday as LINK rose to an intraday high of $27.42 before settling at $26.10. The current session sees LINK in the red as sellers look to drive it below $25. LINK is currently down almost 3% and trading at $25.34.\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Uniswap (UNI) has started the week on a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  note as sellers look to drive it below $15 after an extremely \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  week. UNI registered a sharp increase on Monday, rising over 7% and settling at $13.98. Sellers attempted to lower the price on Tuesday as UNI fell to an intraday low of $13.15. However, it recovered from this level to register an increase of 8.14% to go above $15 and settle at $15.12. UNI surged to an intraday high of $16.52 on Wednesday as buyers attempted a move past resistance levels. However, it could not stay above $16 and fell back, settling at $16.69 after registering an increase of almost 4%. Sellers took control on Thursday after another failed attempt to go above resistance levels. As a result, UNI dropped 4.09% and settled at $15.04.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/tZC4eXFO/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 UNI bounced back on Friday, surging almost 17% to go above the resistance at $16 and settle at $17.58. UNI remained positive over the weekend, rising by 2.43% on Saturday and 3.30% on Sunday despite increasing \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and settled at $18.61. However, the current session sees UNI firmly in the red, with the price down over 5% and trading at $17.65.\par \par \uc2 Celestia (TIA) Price Analysis\par \par \uc2 Celestia (TIA) has registered a substantial decline after failing to go above the resistance at $9. Despite starting the previous week in the red, TIA recovered on Tuesday, rebounding from an intraday low of $7.30, registering an increase of 5.46% and settling at $8.09. TIA rocketed to an intraday high of $8.93 on Wednesday as \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment intensified. However, buyers lost momentum after reaching this level, and TIA fell back to settle at $8.33 after an increase of almost 3%. \b \highlight22\uc2 Volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  persisted on Thursday as TIA rose to an intraday high of $8.70 and fell to an intraday low of $7.86 before settling at $8.24.\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/x/EKci7VR1/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TradingView}}}\par \par \uc2 TIA registered a substantial increase on Friday as \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment returned, rising over 7% and settling at $8.84, still unable to go above $9. Buyers attempted to go past the resistance on Saturday but were unsuccessful, with TIA losing momentum after reaching $9.98. As a result, sellers took over and drove the price down by 4.24% to $8.47. Sellers retained control on Sunday as TIA fell to $8.37 after a drop of 1.11%. \b \highlight22\uc2 Bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment has intensified considerably during the ongoing session, with the price down almost 8% and trading at $7.73.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This article is provided for informational purposes only. It is not offered or intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, financial, or other advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020241210ekc90000t\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Radiant Capital\par \b \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened in crypto today\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Cointelegraph \par \uc2 616 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 December 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Need to know what happened in crypto today? Here is the latest news on daily trends and events impacting Bitcoin price, blockchain, DeFi, NFTs, Web3 and crypto \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvNzhkNzg3NjEtM2JkMi00NTY5LTk2YTctNjJhOTdmMGExYjBh.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened in crypto today }}}\par \par \uc2 Today in crypto, Radiant Capital says a North Korean-aligned attacker was behind the $50 million October hack on its platform, the Cardano Foundation\u8217\'20\'19s X account was hacked to post a phishing scam, and El Salvador\u8217\'20\'19s president says his country has over $330 million in unrealized gains from its Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 Radiant says North Korean posed as ex-contractor in $50 million hack\par \par \uc2 Radiant Capital said on Dec. 6 that the $50 million hack on its platform in October {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/radiant-capital-north-korean-impersonated-ex-contractor-50-million-hack"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was carried out by a North Korea-aligned hacker }}}\uc2  posing as an ex-contractor who sent malware via \uc2 Telegram\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The platform said a Radiant developer received a \uc2 Telegram\uc2  message with a zip file from a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrusted former contractor\u8221\'20\'1D in September, which investigating cybersecurity firm \uc2 Mandiant\uc2  said was \u8220\'20\'1Cattributable to a Democratic People\u8217\'20\'19s Republic of Korea (DPRK)-nexus threat actor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis ZIP file, when shared for feedback among other developers, ultimately delivered malware that facilitated the subsequent intrusion,\u8221\'20\'1D Radiant added.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193a922-1e19-7e08-80de-0f55888b8061"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC, United States, Cybersecurity, Cardano, Hacks, El Salvador, Nayib Bukele, Policy }}}\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RDNTCapital/status/1865201964625035526"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Radiant Capital }}}\par \par \uc2 It believes the actor responsible is known as \u8220\'20\'1CUNC4736,\u8221\'20\'1D also known as \u8220\'20\'1CCitrine Sleet\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 believed to be aligned with North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s main intelligence agency, the Reconnaissance General Bureau (RGB), and speculated to be a sub-cluster of the hacking collective the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/people/top-people-in-crypto-and-blockchain-2023/lazarus-group/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lazarus Group }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Radiant was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/radiant-capital-pauses-contracts-exploit-fears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 forced to halt its lending markets }}}\uc2  on Oct. 16 after an attacker gained control of several signers\u8217\'20\'19 private keys and smart contracts. North Korean hacking groups have long targeted crypto platforms and have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/north-korean-hackers-stolen-crypto"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stolen $3 billion }}}\uc2  in crypto between 2017 and 2023.\par \par \uc2 Cardano Foundation X account hacked\par \par \uc2 The Cardano Foundation\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cardano-foundation-x-account-hacked-scam-links-posted-removed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 X account was hacked }}}\uc2  on Dec. 8 by a threat actor who posted malicious links on the Foundation\u8217\'20\'19s social media page.\par \par \uc2 Initially, the hacker created a post advertising a fraudulent token called \u8220\'20\'1CADAsol,\u8221\'20\'1D which managed to rack up approximately $500,000 in trading volume before collapsing.\par \par \uc2 Following the promotion of the fake token, the hacker created a second fraudulent post claiming that the Cardano Foundation would drop support for \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) due to scrutiny from the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193a7c1-9753-7778-9fcf-c76766840056"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC, United States, Cybersecurity, Cardano, Hacks, El Salvador, Nayib Bukele, Policy }}}\par \par \uc2 One of the fraudulent posts from the Cardano Foundation\u8217\'20\'19s compromised X account. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.me/investigations/189"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ZackXBT }}}\par \par \uc2 Both posts have since been deleted, and the Cardano Foundation is working on regaining control of the social media account.\par \par \uc2 However, users are encouraged to stay clear of the account and not to interact with any links from the Cardano Foundation X page until the issue is fully resolved.\par \par \uc2 El Salvador\u8217\'20\'19s Bitcoin gains top $300 million\par \par \uc2 Salvadoran President \uc2 Nayib Bukele{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/el-salvador-bitcoin-holdings-unrealized-gains"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highlighted the country\u8217\'20\'19s unrealized gains }}}\uc2  from its Bitcoin investments on social media after the cryptocurrency surpassed $100,000 for the first time.\par \par \uc2 On Dec. 5, Bitcoin ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC }}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-hits-100-000-first-time-new-all-time-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached $100,000 for the first time }}}\uc2 , sparking celebrations within the crypto community. That same day, Autism Capital, a crypto-focused account on X, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AutismCapital/status/1864505429512028251"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked }}}\uc2  Bukele to share El Salvador\u8217\'20\'19s Bitcoin portfolio to \u8220\'20\'1Cdunk on the haters.\u8221\'20\'1D Bukele responded by posting the country\u8217\'20\'19s BTC holdings on X.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193a672-5ae4-74ac-a0c4-dcb51d26be7b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Telegram, United States, Pavel Durov, Memecoin, Policy }}}\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/nayibbukele/status/1864506095131144278"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nayib Bukele }}}\par \par \uc2 Bukele\u8217\'20\'19s latest update shows the country has spent nearly $270 million on Bitcoin since its initial adoption of the cryptocurrency. The portfolio shows no Bitcoin has been sold, and unrealized gains now exceed $333 million.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvNzhkNzg3NjEtM2JkMi00NTY5LTk2YTctNjJhOTdmMGExYjBh.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020241209ekc800009\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 El Salvador\par \b \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened in crypto today\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Cointelegraph \par \uc2 638 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 December 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Need to know what happened in crypto today? Here is the latest news on daily trends and events impacting Bitcoin price, blockchain, DeFi, NFTs, Web3 and crypto \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvNzhkNzg3NjEtM2JkMi00NTY5LTk2YTctNjJhOTdmMGExYjBh.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened in crypto today }}}\par \par \uc2 Today in crypto, the Cardano Foundation\u8217\'20\'19s X account was hacked, El Salvador is sitting on unrealized gains of more than $330 million on its Bitcoin investment, according to the country\u8217\'20\'19s president, and several crypto industry executives have voiced frustration over \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  Commissioner \uc2 Caroline Crenshaw\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s looming renomination date.\par \par \uc2 Cardano Foundation X account hacked\par \par \uc2 The Cardano Foundation's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cardano-foundation-x-account-hacked-scam-links-posted-removed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 X account was hacked }}}\uc2  on Dec. 8 by a threat actor who posted malicious links on the Foundation's social media page.\par \par \uc2 Initially, the hacker created a post advertising a fraudulent token called "ADAsol", which managed to rack up approximately $500,000 in trading volume before collapsing.\par \par \uc2 Following the promotion of the fake token, the hacker created a second fraudulent post claiming that the Cardano Foundation would drop support for \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) due to scrutiny from the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193a7c1-9753-7778-9fcf-c76766840056"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC, United States, Cybersecurity, Cardano, Hacks, El Salvador, Nayib Bukele, Policy }}}\par \par \uc2 One of the fraudulent posts from the Cardano Foundation\u8217\'20\'19s compromised X account. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.me/investigations/189"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ZackXBT }}}\par \par \uc2 Both posts have since been deleted, and the Cardano Foundation is working on regaining control of the social media account.\par \par \uc2 However, users are encouraged to stay clear of the account and not to interact with any links from the Cardano Foundation X page until the issue is fully resolved.\par \par \uc2 El Salvador\u8217\'20\'19s Bitcoin gains top $300 million\par \par \uc2 Salvadoran President \uc2 Nayib Bukele{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/el-salvador-bitcoin-holdings-unrealized-gains"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highlighted the country\u8217\'20\'19s unrealized gains }}}\uc2  from its Bitcoin investments on social media after the cryptocurrency surpassed $100,000 for the first time.\par \par \uc2 On Dec. 5, Bitcoin ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC }}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-hits-100-000-first-time-new-all-time-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached $100,000 for the first time }}}\uc2 , sparking celebrations within the crypto community. That same day, Autism Capital, a crypto-focused account on X, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AutismCapital/status/1864505429512028251"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked }}}\uc2  Bukele to share El Salvador\u8217\'20\'19s Bitcoin portfolio to \u8220\'20\'1Cdunk on the haters.\u8221\'20\'1D Bukele responded by posting the country\u8217\'20\'19s BTC holdings on X.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193a672-5ae4-74ac-a0c4-dcb51d26be7b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Telegram, United States, Pavel Durov, Memecoin, Policy }}}\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/nayibbukele/status/1864506095131144278"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nayib Bukele }}}\par \par \uc2 Bukele\u8217\'20\'19s latest update shows the country has spent nearly $270 million on Bitcoin since its initial adoption of the cryptocurrency. The portfolio shows no Bitcoin has been sold, and unrealized gains now exceed $333 million.\par \par \uc2 Crypto industry fears \u8220\'20\'1Cvehemently anti crypto\u8221\'20\'1D Caroline Crenshaw SEC vote\par \par \uc2 The US Senate Banking Committee will vote on Dec. 11 whether to renominate SEC Commissioner \uc2 Caroline Crenshaw\uc2 , a vocal crypto skeptic. Several industry executives have voiced frustration over the possibility of her reelection.\par \par \uc2 Crenshaw was one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-etf-approval-critics-lash-sec-decision-fraud-manipulation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two SEC commissioners to vote against }}}\uc2  the approval of spot Bitcoin ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC }}}\uc2  ) exchange-traded funds (ETF) in January.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Caroline Crenshaw\uc2  is anti-crypto. She even embarrassingly opposed Bitcoin ETFs. The SEC has to change,\u8221\'20\'1D crypto exchange \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  president and chief operating officer \uc2 Emilie Choi\uc2  said in a Dec. 7 X {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/emiliemc/status/1865191039495024804"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post }}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/0193a4dc-9772-7822-b5db-5435f9b8e0e9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Telegram, United States, Pavel Durov, Memecoin, Policy }}}\par \par \uc2 Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AlexanderGrieve/status/1865108479737761977"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alexander Grieve }}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto investment firm Paradigm government affairs vice president Alexander Grieve {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AlexanderGrieve/status/1865108479737761977"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  it was \u8220\'20\'1Cone last \u8220\'20\'1Cgift\u8221\'20\'1D for crypto on the way out the door, Senate Banking Chair Sherrod Brown is trying to ram through the renomination of anti-crypto SEC commissioner \uc2 Caroline Crenshaw\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg ETF analyst James Seyffart said in a Dec. 7 X {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JSeyff/status/1865147022812049635"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post that }}}\uc2  Crenshaw wasn\u8217\'20\'19t just \u8220\'20\'1Can ally\u8221\'20\'1D to SEC chair and crypto skeptic \uc2 Gary Gensler\uc2  but was even more \u8220\'20\'1Cvehemently anti-crypto\u8221\'20\'1D than Gensler himself.\par \par \uc2 Following the SEC approving the spot Bitcoin ETFs in the United States on Jan. 10, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-commissioner-anti-crypto-replacement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crenshaw, who was sworn in }}}\uc2  as an SEC commissioner in August 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-approved-spot-bitcoin-etfs-week-law-decoded-jan-8-15"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said that the agency\u8217\'20\'19s move to greenlight }}}\uc2  the ETFs was \u8220\'20\'1Cunsound and ahistorical.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMDgvNzhkNzg3NjEtM2JkMi00NTY5LTk2YTctNjJhOTdmMGExYjBh.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020241208ekc8000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
