ations alongside platforms like Ethereum and Cardano. It stands out by enabling faster transactions without relying on sharding or second-layer solutions. Solana's native cryptocurrency, SOL, is central to its ecosystem, facilitating transactions, powering programs, and rewarding network participants. The platform supports development across multiple programming languages, making it flexible for developers. With its high-capacity network designed for hosting high-activity products and services, Solana has potential in the blockchain space. In the current market cycle, its emphasis on scalability and performance makes it a noteworthy option for developers and users interested in decentralized applications.\par \par \uc2 XRP: A Fast, Decentralized Cryptocurrency for Borderless Transactions\par \par \uc2 XRP is a cryptocurrency supported by the XRP Ledger, designed to enable fast, low-cost, and borderless transactions. Operating on a decentralized system without a central authority, XRP ensures secure and irreversible transfers without the need for a bank account. Created by Jed McCaleb, Arthur Britto, and David Schwartz, it was launched with an initial supply of 100 billion, with 80 billion gifted to Ripple for development. Ripple uses XRP to enhance network liquidity, placing 55 billion XRP in escrow for controlled release. XRP aims to facilitate seamless payment transfers across currencies. In the current market cycle, XRP's efficient technology and potential for widespread adoption may make it an attractive option for users.\par \par \uc2 Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ): A Sustainable Blockchain with High Scalability\par \par \uc2 Cardano is a blockchain platform that supports smart contracts for decentralized apps, tokens, and games. Its cryptocurrency, \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , competes with Ethereum's ETH, allowing users to store value, make payments, and stake on the network. Cardano uses a more energy-efficient method called proof-of-stake, making it more sustainable than platforms that use proof-of-work. The blockchain is divided into two layers: one for transactions and one for smart contracts, improving its speed and scalability. This design enables it to potentially process up to a million transactions per second. Introduced in 2021, Cardano's tokens offer secure and low-fee interactions. With these features, \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strong potential in the current market cycle.\par \par \uc2 Conclusion\par \par \uc2 While SOL, XRP, and \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  show limited short-term potential, DOGEN stands out. Designed for those pursuing excellence, it embodies luxury and success. With an expected 700% growth by the end of its presale, DOGEN could see thousand-fold returns this altcoin season. Following tokens like BONK, WIF, and Popcat, it aims for record-breaking success, offering real benefits and exclusive perks for early adopters.\par \par \uc2 Site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dogen.meme/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://dogen.meme/}}}\par \par \uc2 Twitter: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/dogenmeme"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://x.com/dogenmeme}}}\par \par \uc2 Telegram: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.me/Dogen_Portal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.me/Dogen_Portal}}}\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This is a sponsored press release and is for informational purposes only. It does not reflect the views of Crypto Daily, nor is it intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, or financial advice.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cryptodaily.co.uk/investment-disclaimer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Investment Disclaimer}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020241207ekc60000e\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 markets\par \b \uc2 Cardano price gains 88% \u8212\'20\'14 Is the  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2  rally just getting started?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Marcel Pechman \par \uc2 755 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 December 2024\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2024. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Cardano price soared as its open interest increased. Is it time for a correction, or can \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  price go higher?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMTIvMDE5MzhlMDEtOGM4OS03OGQ1LThmYmItODU3ZmY3YjkyYzhj.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cardano price gains 88% \u8212\'20\'14 Is the \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22  rally just getting started? }}}\par \par \uc2 Cardano ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) surged by 88.8% between Nov. 18 and Dec. 3, reaching its highest price in nearly three years at $1.33. This rally mirrored broader gains in the altcoin market, which reached a peak of $1.52 trillion on Dec. 3, up from $1.16 trillion on Nov. 18.\par \par \uc2 The 15-day \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally was accompanied by an all-time high in leveraged positions using futures contracts, prompting traders to question whether the dip to $1.16 on Dec. 3 presents a buying opportunity and to evaluate the potential risk of cascading liquidations.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/01938e01-83a2-7912-a849-cf741a566066"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Funding, Markets, Leverage, Cardano, Futures, Solana }}}\par \par \uc2 Altcoin market cap, USD (red) vs. \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD (blue). Source: TradingView / Cointelegraph\par \par \uc2 Cardano, along with Stellar ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/stellar-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XLM }}}\uc2  ), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP }}}\uc2 , Algorand (ALGO), and IOTA, were among the best-performing top-100 cryptocurrencies during the 15-day period ending Dec. 3. Some analysts have referred to this movement as the \u8220\'20\'1Cdino coins rally,\u8221\'20\'1D as these altcoins have experienced at least two prior cycles of boom and bust.\par \par \uc2 What stands out about Cardano, aside from the impressive price gain, is the 37% increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  open interest on derivatives exchanges, surpassing the previous peak from October 2022. The aggregate exposure of leveraged longs (buyers) and shorts (sellers) totaled 932.5 million \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Dec. 3, equivalent to $1.2 billion.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/01938e01-c26e-75ab-b4be-f8c5fe0d32e7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Funding, Markets, Leverage, Cardano, Futures, Solana }}}\par \par \uc2 Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) futures open interest, \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Source: CoinGlass\par \par \uc2 For comparison, the aggregate futures open interest for BNB stands at $1.08 billion, despite the BNB Chain market capitalization being more than twice the size of Cardano's. Additionally, open interest in altcoins like Solana ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL }}}\uc2  ), Dogecoin ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE }}}\uc2  ), and Avalanche ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX }}}\uc2  ) remains below their previous all-time highs.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures reflect modest optimism and low liquidation risks\par \par \uc2 The surge in demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures should not be viewed as inherently \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  or \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as these contracts have corresponding positions on the other side of the trade. To gauge traders' sentiment, one should monitor the monthly futures contracts premium, also known as the basis rate. In healthy markets, annualized premiums between 5% and 10% are typical.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/01938e02-0ef0-7464-86b8-fa926b3626bc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Funding, Markets, Leverage, Cardano, Futures, Solana }}}\par \par \uc2 Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) 3-month futures annualized premium. Source: Laevitas.ch\par \par \uc2 Cardano's monthly futures contracts have been trading at a healthy 17% premium relative to the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  price, consistent with previous bull markets and not considered unusual. During periods of excessive confidence, longs may pay up to 60% annualized for leverage, a significant cost for longer-term positions.\par \par \uc2 It is also important to consider the perpetual contracts. In these cases, exchanges charge either longs or shorts a fee for excessive leverage to balance risk. Given that crypto traders are typically \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a monthly fee ranging from 0.5% to 2.1% is generally charged to longs.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/01938e02-5275-735c-ab61-159f41fd1cd6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Funding, Markets, Leverage, Cardano, Futures, Solana }}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  perpetual futures 8-hour funding rate. Source: Laevitas.ch\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  perpetual futures funding rate peaked at 6% per month on Dec. 2 and Dec. 3 but has since decreased to 2.2%. This suggests that traders initially used excessive leverage for a short period but subsequently deposited additional funds to mitigate risk.\par \par \uc2 Lastly, it is important to consider the total value locked (TVL) on the Cardano network, as increased demand for smart contract processing is a key factor driving sustainable \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2024-12/01938e02-8e5f-791c-b09c-eb1212e40886"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrencies, Funding, Markets, Leverage, Cardano, Futures, Solana }}}\par \par \uc2 Cardano network total value locked (TVL), \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Source: DefiLlama\par \par \uc2 Cardano remains a relatively small player in the decentralized applications (DApps) ecosystem, with $685 million in deposits. In comparison, Aptos holds $1.23 billion in TVL, and Avalanche totals $1.53 billion. More notably, there has been no growth in Cardano's TVL over the past few months.\par \par \uc2 Given the neutral-to-\b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  funding rate and futures premium, there is no indication that the increased demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures is the primary driver of the price surge. Therefore, there is no immediate risk of cascading liquidations.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/images/840_aHR0cHM6Ly9zMy5jb2ludGVsZWdyYXBoLmNvbS91cGxvYWRzLzIwMjQtMTIvMDE5MzhlMDEtOGM4OS03OGQ1LThmYmItODU3ZmY3YjkyYzhj.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image. }}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020241203ekc3000e3\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clb